1
00:00:03,510 --> 00:00:05,210
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:18,179
(After the 4 siblings' memorable 1st dinner together)

3
00:00:18,352 --> 00:00:19,652
- Sun Young.
- Yes?

4
00:00:19,836 --> 00:00:22,096
- Are you tired?
- I'm not tired at all.

5
00:00:22,296 --> 00:00:23,706
- How about a round of omok?
- What?

6
00:00:23,731 --> 00:00:25,291
- How about a round of omok?
- Sure.

7
00:00:25,436 --> 00:00:27,006
- You say that you hardly lose.
- I'm really good at it.

8
00:00:28,376 --> 00:00:29,976
It's hard for you to lose, right?

9
00:00:29,976 --> 00:00:32,506
- Are you good at omok?
- Omok? No way.

10
00:00:33,006 --> 00:00:34,276
I'm seriously good at omok.

11
00:00:34,916 --> 00:00:36,376
I don't think I can lose at omok.

12
00:00:36,716 --> 00:00:38,186
He says that he can't lose at omok.

13
00:00:38,616 --> 00:00:39,856
- I'm good at omok.
- If I win, you have to pay me...

14
00:00:39,856 --> 00:00:40,986
- Me too.
- I'm good at omok.

15
00:00:41,056 --> 00:00:42,516
I'm quite good at omok too.

16
00:00:42,586 --> 00:00:44,326
- I'm good at omok.
- If I win...

17
00:00:44,326 --> 00:00:45,356
Me too.

18
00:00:45,356 --> 00:00:46,856
Is there a go board here?

19
00:00:47,456 --> 00:00:48,796
There is.

20
00:00:48,796 --> 00:00:50,266
I saw it as soon as I got here.

21
00:00:50,266 --> 00:00:51,296
I see.

22
00:00:51,296 --> 00:00:52,996
(Who will win the match between these self-proclaimed omok masters?)

23
00:00:53,336 --> 00:00:55,296
(The game of omok starts.)

24
00:00:57,866 --> 00:01:00,836
(The two omok masters are taking the game seriously.)

25
00:01:00,836 --> 00:01:02,006
You've got a nice vibe.

26
00:01:02,136 --> 00:01:04,306
This is the most serious I've seen you all day.

27
00:01:04,306 --> 00:01:05,506
(Roh Yoon Seo watching from the sidelines)

28
00:01:05,506 --> 00:01:06,576
I must win.

29
00:01:07,176 --> 00:01:08,946
- Now...
- You're good at it.

30
00:01:09,446 --> 00:01:10,616
I should watch and learn.

31
00:01:10,616 --> 00:01:12,286
- You're actually quite good.
- You too.

32
00:01:13,286 --> 00:01:15,756
(About 30 minutes later)

33
00:01:16,056 --> 00:01:17,326
(Pouting)

34
00:01:17,326 --> 00:01:18,886
(Keeping a poker face behind his sunglasses)

35
00:01:19,956 --> 00:01:22,556
Where did you study?

36
00:01:23,026 --> 00:01:24,396
Here and there.

37
00:01:24,566 --> 00:01:25,796
I studied near Mount Jiri.

38
00:01:25,826 --> 00:01:26,936
- Mount Jiri?
- Yes.

39
00:01:27,036 --> 00:01:28,466
Since I'm from Gangwon Province, I studied at Mount Seorak.

40
00:01:29,066 --> 00:01:30,606
Places like Mount Seorak and Mount Taebaek.

41
00:01:30,706 --> 00:01:31,906
That's some serious training ground.

42
00:01:34,506 --> 00:01:36,106
(Sliding)

43
00:01:38,676 --> 00:01:39,806
(Laughing triumphantly)

44
00:01:39,806 --> 00:01:40,816
What's going on?

45
00:01:40,816 --> 00:01:42,116
(Is it finally over?)

46
00:01:42,116 --> 00:01:43,116
Did you win?

47
00:01:43,116 --> 00:01:44,286
That's incredible.

48
00:01:44,286 --> 00:01:45,286
- Goodness.
- This is four...

49
00:01:45,286 --> 00:01:46,616
(It's a 4-3.)

50
00:01:49,116 --> 00:01:50,886
(Sun Young from Mount Jiri wins.)

51
00:01:50,886 --> 00:01:52,526
Is it because of this?

52
00:01:52,526 --> 00:01:53,896
(Sun Young from Mount Jiri wins.)

53
00:01:54,356 --> 00:01:55,826
- Sun Young, you're good.
- You're quite good.

54
00:01:55,826 --> 00:01:57,426
- Let's play once more.
- I've never lost before.

55
00:01:57,426 --> 00:01:58,466
Seriously?

56
00:01:58,666 --> 00:02:01,096
- Let's play 1 more round.
- There are 2 masters on our team.

57
00:02:01,096 --> 00:02:02,896
(Round 2)

58
00:02:03,036 --> 00:02:05,236
I bet I'll lose again.

59
00:02:05,406 --> 00:02:07,936
- Please let me win this time.
- Watch out.

60
00:02:07,936 --> 00:02:09,176
(The game speeds up.)

61
00:02:10,206 --> 00:02:11,206
(Tap)

62
00:02:11,676 --> 00:02:13,676
(You Seok places what he believes is the winning move.)

63
00:02:14,216 --> 00:02:16,376
What? I didn't see that before.

64
00:02:21,716 --> 00:02:25,226
(Pure happiness)

65
00:02:25,386 --> 00:02:26,426
(You Seok from Mount Seorak wins.)

66
00:02:26,426 --> 00:02:28,026
- You did a good job.
- I did well.

67
00:02:28,026 --> 00:02:30,326
I know. I didn't even see it.

68
00:02:31,596 --> 00:02:33,266
It was another 4-3.

69
00:02:33,366 --> 00:02:35,896
You're very good at it now.

70
00:02:35,966 --> 00:02:36,966
This is perfect.

71
00:02:36,966 --> 00:02:38,206
Anyway,

72
00:02:38,206 --> 00:02:39,436
today's score is 1 to 1.

73
00:02:40,106 --> 00:02:41,106
(Moaning)

74
00:02:41,236 --> 00:02:43,306
- Mister.
- The game was enjoyable today.

75
00:02:43,306 --> 00:02:44,406
It had a good impact on you.

76
00:02:44,976 --> 00:02:46,646
- Mount Seorak, I mean.
- It was a good game.

77
00:02:46,876 --> 00:02:48,576
It must be the spirit of Gangwon Province.

78
00:02:50,946 --> 00:02:53,146
- What do you think of the vibe?
- Oh, my.

79
00:02:53,146 --> 00:02:55,686
I changed the atmosphere a little. Isn't it nice?

80
00:02:57,086 --> 00:03:00,596
When you film with this, it looks like we're in an old movie.

81
00:03:00,596 --> 00:03:02,396
- It's rolling.
- Yes.

82
00:03:02,396 --> 00:03:05,196
(Their first night in Tongyeong)

83
00:03:05,196 --> 00:03:06,296
It's rolling.

84
00:03:06,296 --> 00:03:08,096
(Jung Ah and Yoon Seo)

85
00:03:08,596 --> 00:03:10,606
(This time, she puts on a face mask and grabs the microphone.)

86
00:03:11,266 --> 00:03:15,036
(Late-night karaoke begins.)

87
00:03:15,036 --> 00:03:18,646
(Among the crowd)

88
00:03:18,646 --> 00:03:20,146
(To me, you are)

89
00:03:20,146 --> 00:03:21,876
Oh, come on.

90
00:03:22,346 --> 00:03:24,616
(They're playing another game.)

91
00:03:24,616 --> 00:03:27,686
What? That's nonsense.

92
00:03:27,686 --> 00:03:29,116
(Together and apart,)

93
00:03:29,116 --> 00:03:30,556
(the 4 siblings settle into their 1st night together.)

94
00:03:31,256 --> 00:03:32,526
(Wiggling)

95
00:03:32,526 --> 00:03:34,556
There he is. Go on and sing.

96
00:03:34,956 --> 00:03:36,356
- Aren't you going to sing?
- No.

97
00:03:36,896 --> 00:03:39,726
When is the performance? The dance goes like this.

98
00:03:39,726 --> 00:03:40,796
(Being totally cute)

99
00:03:40,796 --> 00:03:41,996
You're a goof ball.

100
00:03:42,466 --> 00:03:43,566
You're a goof ball.

101
00:03:44,206 --> 00:03:46,706
- He's like our baby brother.
- He's a little rascal.

102
00:03:47,076 --> 00:03:50,006
You Seok doesn't act cute with just anyone.

103
00:03:50,676 --> 00:03:51,676
Right?

104
00:03:51,846 --> 00:03:53,616
- He's like a cat.
- He doesn't act cute...

105
00:03:53,616 --> 00:03:54,776
- with just anyone.
- He's a cat.

106
00:03:54,776 --> 00:03:56,146
(His cuteness is reserved for his older siblings.)

107
00:03:56,146 --> 00:03:57,446
You'd better not let me hear you...

108
00:03:57,446 --> 00:03:59,316
acting cute with anyone else.

109
00:03:59,316 --> 00:04:01,856
(The eldest gets strict about his acting cute.)

110
00:04:02,086 --> 00:04:03,186
You hear me?

111
00:04:03,356 --> 00:04:06,086
My goal is to win you all over.

112
00:04:06,326 --> 00:04:07,496
That's what I'd like.

113
00:04:07,626 --> 00:04:08,696
- Like last time?
- By acting cute?

114
00:04:08,696 --> 00:04:10,366
Like when you made us laugh on the boat?

115
00:04:10,366 --> 00:04:11,666
That's just...

116
00:04:12,166 --> 00:04:13,836
- the tip of the iceberg.
- That was...

117
00:04:13,836 --> 00:04:14,966
(Captain Kang was the tip of the iceberg.)

118
00:04:14,966 --> 00:04:17,366
- He was gross.
- It was 1 out of 10.

119
00:04:19,106 --> 00:04:20,306
"Gross?"

120
00:04:20,306 --> 00:04:22,336
- You're being very honest again.
- I don't like men like him.

121
00:04:22,436 --> 00:04:23,876
I hate men like him.

122
00:04:23,876 --> 00:04:26,176
(Laughing)

123
00:04:26,306 --> 00:04:28,516
I will never forget him.

124
00:04:29,916 --> 00:04:31,646
- Let's go to bed.
- Please go ahead.

125
00:04:31,746 --> 00:04:33,086
Aren't you going to bed?

126
00:04:33,086 --> 00:04:34,416
I will after I clean up.

127
00:04:35,486 --> 00:04:39,856
(Wrapping things up with a clean finish)

128
00:04:41,456 --> 00:04:42,796
I'm going out for a walk.

129
00:04:45,166 --> 00:04:48,296
(Not quite ready to call it a night)

130
00:04:48,296 --> 00:04:51,506
(The youngest two head out for a late-night walk.)

131
00:04:51,706 --> 00:04:52,766
Look at the stars.

132
00:04:55,106 --> 00:04:56,976
We can see the stars.

133
00:04:56,976 --> 00:04:58,146
- There are so many.
- We can see the stars.

134
00:04:59,606 --> 00:05:03,616
(The night sky is blanketed with stars.)

135
00:05:04,086 --> 00:05:05,346
That's a constellation.

136
00:05:05,846 --> 00:05:07,586
- Isn't that the Cassiopeia?
- Where?

137
00:05:08,016 --> 00:05:11,326
It's right here. The one that looks like this.

138
00:05:12,286 --> 00:05:13,896
Look over here.

139
00:05:14,926 --> 00:05:16,056
It's the Big Dipper.

140
00:05:16,056 --> 00:05:17,866
- Really?
- It's shaped like a ladle.

141
00:05:18,496 --> 00:05:20,266
You can see the Big Dipper so clearly.

142
00:05:20,696 --> 00:05:21,896
Let's go to the rooftop.

143
00:05:25,566 --> 00:05:26,836
Will we get a better view up there?

144
00:05:32,746 --> 00:05:36,946
(The ocean stretches out in full view even at the rooftop.)

145
00:05:42,256 --> 00:05:47,226
(They capture the moment under the sky overflowing with stars.)

146
00:05:47,456 --> 00:05:49,926
Brush your teeth out here. It feels more special this way.

147
00:05:51,266 --> 00:05:52,966
I feel like I'm at my grandmother's house.

148
00:05:55,466 --> 00:05:56,466
Yes.

149
00:05:56,936 --> 00:05:58,936
We can see the sea from here,

150
00:05:59,306 --> 00:06:01,436
and the weather is perfect.

151
00:06:02,806 --> 00:06:04,976
(Their first night in Tongyeong comes to an end.)

152
00:06:04,976 --> 00:06:08,016
(It's too beautiful to sleep through.)

153
00:06:10,246 --> 00:06:14,016
(The darkness slowly fades.)

154
00:06:15,686 --> 00:06:18,486
(A new day dawns over Tongyeong.)

155
00:06:19,256 --> 00:06:21,956
(The sea is the first to wake.)

156
00:06:21,956 --> 00:06:24,366
(As the harbour comes to life,)

157
00:06:25,096 --> 00:06:29,566
(the fishing village slowly begins another day.)

158
00:06:30,736 --> 00:06:33,706
(What adventures await us today?)

159
00:06:34,936 --> 00:06:36,176
(Current time: 6am)

160
00:06:36,176 --> 00:06:38,376
(Sun Young gets up.)

161
00:06:41,146 --> 00:06:44,316
(Starting the morning with stretching)

162
00:06:45,486 --> 00:06:47,916
(Kicking off the day with a productive morning routine)

163
00:06:48,286 --> 00:06:50,486
(Even with a spacious living room,)

164
00:06:50,486 --> 00:06:54,326
(she still ends up settling in the kitchen.)

165
00:06:55,196 --> 00:06:57,596
(Peeling and enjoying Korean melon for breakfast)

166
00:06:59,896 --> 00:07:03,866
(Savouring a relaxing cup of coffee)

167
00:07:05,736 --> 00:07:08,606
(Did she find something?)

168
00:07:11,846 --> 00:07:14,376
(Eating)

169
00:07:15,576 --> 00:07:18,746
(Sneaking bites of the crew's snacks from the corner of the yard)

170
00:07:20,456 --> 00:07:23,886
(One isn't enough. It's time to raid another snack.)

171
00:07:25,356 --> 00:07:27,896
(The wrapper disappears neatly into her pocket.)

172
00:07:28,696 --> 00:07:32,526
(When Sun Young wakes up early, she eats a lot of snacks.)

173
00:07:33,736 --> 00:07:35,166
(Soon, Jung Ah gets up.)

174
00:07:35,166 --> 00:07:36,636
- Jung Ah.
- What are you...

175
00:07:37,766 --> 00:07:41,076
(Yoon Seo also gets up.)

176
00:07:42,576 --> 00:07:44,276
- Did you sleep well?
- Why did you get up so early?

177
00:07:44,276 --> 00:07:45,776
(Crawling)

178
00:07:45,976 --> 00:07:48,746
You look cute. You're cuter in the morning.

179
00:07:51,346 --> 00:07:52,386
Jung Ah.

180
00:07:54,186 --> 00:07:55,286
What else should I know?

181
00:07:55,286 --> 00:07:57,986
Did you eat some Korean melon this morning?

182
00:07:58,326 --> 00:07:59,626
I had coffee,

183
00:07:59,726 --> 00:08:03,326
and I ate two of the snacks the production crew had hidden.

184
00:08:03,326 --> 00:08:04,326
Snacks?

185
00:08:04,326 --> 00:08:06,866
I raided the crew's snack stash.

186
00:08:06,866 --> 00:08:08,566
- Where did you find it?
- In the flower bed.

187
00:08:08,566 --> 00:08:09,736
You're better than me.

188
00:08:09,736 --> 00:08:12,706
- I didn't even know it existed.
- In the flower bed.

189
00:08:13,136 --> 00:08:15,436
I woke up at 6am.

190
00:08:15,976 --> 00:08:17,376
I had nothing to do.

191
00:08:17,746 --> 00:08:18,806
I was really bored.

192
00:08:19,346 --> 00:08:21,176
- They should've given us books.
- Right.

193
00:08:21,176 --> 00:08:23,346
- There was nothing to do.
- Why didn't you go back to sleep?

194
00:08:23,646 --> 00:08:24,646
(You Seok wakes up.)

195
00:08:24,646 --> 00:08:26,416
Sun Young, do you want to borrow my books?

196
00:08:28,256 --> 00:08:30,356
(He brings out books that he packed.)

197
00:08:30,356 --> 00:08:32,786
Gosh, look at him. I don't believe you.

198
00:08:33,226 --> 00:08:35,626
Gosh, look at him. I don't believe you.

199
00:08:35,726 --> 00:08:38,026
- Have you read them?
- I've been reading this book.

200
00:08:38,026 --> 00:08:39,296
Really? That's incredible.

201
00:08:39,296 --> 00:08:41,636
- This is unbelievable.
- Then you can read this.

202
00:08:42,196 --> 00:08:43,266
Jung Ah, look at him.

203
00:08:43,266 --> 00:08:44,336
(The two of them have been reading the same book.)

204
00:08:44,336 --> 00:08:46,506
You Seok brought this. Isn't that funny?

205
00:08:46,506 --> 00:08:48,376
You two really seem to click.

206
00:08:48,376 --> 00:08:49,376
(He also feels good.)

207
00:08:50,476 --> 00:08:52,776
(Sun Young gets ready to prepare the ingredients for breakfast.)

208
00:08:52,776 --> 00:08:54,946
All right, shall I start?

209
00:08:55,816 --> 00:08:57,146
I have to keep talking...

210
00:08:57,916 --> 00:09:00,416
to the viewers so there's no awkward silence.

211
00:09:00,416 --> 00:09:01,416
("Kim Sun Young's AM Plaza")

212
00:09:01,756 --> 00:09:03,956
Hello, everyone. From early morning, we're cooking...

213
00:09:04,456 --> 00:09:06,186
delicious food before heading out to earn a living.

214
00:09:08,196 --> 00:09:11,526
Isn't this the dream? In the countryside yard...

215
00:09:11,996 --> 00:09:13,296
What do you call this? A sink.

216
00:09:13,996 --> 00:09:16,836
I can't block the camera. You all have to see it.

217
00:09:18,206 --> 00:09:20,906
(The communication expert turns her back to the camera anyway.)

218
00:09:21,176 --> 00:09:23,806
I'm going to blanch the squid, so a quick...

219
00:09:25,476 --> 00:09:26,506
rinse will do.

220
00:09:26,506 --> 00:09:27,646
(Washing the squid quickly before blanching)

221
00:09:27,846 --> 00:09:28,876
This is...

222
00:09:29,476 --> 00:09:30,486
trash.

223
00:09:31,546 --> 00:09:32,616
(Washing the vegetables)

224
00:09:32,616 --> 00:09:35,056
If I turn up the water,

225
00:09:35,056 --> 00:09:37,256
the camera director will get soaked.

226
00:09:37,256 --> 00:09:38,686
This is how you wash it clean.

227
00:09:40,186 --> 00:09:41,456
It's not bad, right?

228
00:09:42,156 --> 00:09:43,226
That's done.

229
00:09:44,296 --> 00:09:45,366
I'll wash this too.

230
00:09:45,366 --> 00:09:46,596
(When Jung Ah arrives)

231
00:09:46,796 --> 00:09:47,836
Here you go.

232
00:09:47,836 --> 00:09:49,996
Just leave it there. Let me get some water.

233
00:09:53,106 --> 00:09:56,636
We used to wash our hair here and splash water on our necks.

234
00:09:56,636 --> 00:09:57,646
(She can't resist for long.)

235
00:09:57,846 --> 00:09:59,246
All right, like this.

236
00:09:59,246 --> 00:10:00,416
(It's a full-blown water show.)

237
00:10:00,416 --> 00:10:02,646
You need a strong stream of water.

238
00:10:03,716 --> 00:10:04,786
You can rinse it roughly...

239
00:10:06,116 --> 00:10:07,916
when Jung Ah isn't looking.

240
00:10:08,756 --> 00:10:10,756
I'll peel the potatoes, so they can be washed roughly.

241
00:10:10,756 --> 00:10:13,586
- Who are you talking to?
- I'm talking to the viewers.

242
00:10:13,996 --> 00:10:16,926
Stop talking to the viewers and talk to us instead.

243
00:10:16,926 --> 00:10:19,966
I'm washing the vegetables according to Jung Ah's orders.

244
00:10:19,966 --> 00:10:22,196
- Aren't you going to wash these?
- Shall I...

245
00:10:22,196 --> 00:10:23,536
- I washed them all.
- Wash these too.

246
00:10:23,536 --> 00:10:25,166
("Kim Sun Young's AM Plaza" ends abruptly.)

247
00:10:26,036 --> 00:10:28,136
(The preparations continue.)

248
00:10:28,136 --> 00:10:30,176
(What's on the siblings' breakfast menu?)

249
00:10:30,176 --> 00:10:31,976
We're going to make chungmu gimbap.

250
00:10:33,476 --> 00:10:39,246
(Along with fresh seafood)

251
00:10:40,416 --> 00:10:42,786
(A dish that represents Tongyeong)

252
00:10:42,786 --> 00:10:45,226
(Chungmu gimbap)

253
00:10:46,156 --> 00:10:48,526
(When the gimbap fishermen used to take on their boats spoiled fast)

254
00:10:49,126 --> 00:10:50,666
(Radish and cabbage kimchi, squid and fishcake, gimbap)

255
00:10:50,666 --> 00:10:56,366
(It originated from packing the rice and side dishes separately.)

256
00:10:57,136 --> 00:10:59,406
(To go with the siblings' chungmu gimbap)

257
00:10:59,406 --> 00:11:01,236
Chungmu gimbap...

258
00:11:01,606 --> 00:11:04,176
