516
00:21:56,856 --> 00:21:59,426
(Everyone reaches for the chungmu gimbap first.)

517
00:21:59,796 --> 00:22:03,396
- Pit-a-pat. It looks delicious.
- Do I wrap this with...

518
00:22:03,396 --> 00:22:04,536
With rice.

519
00:22:05,936 --> 00:22:09,236
(Yoon Seo also takes a bite.)

520
00:22:09,276 --> 00:22:10,536
- It's good.
- Yes.

521
00:22:10,536 --> 00:22:13,176
(Everyone takes a big bite of the chungmu gimbap.)

522
00:22:13,176 --> 00:22:14,206
With some squid.

523
00:22:15,046 --> 00:22:17,146
(Walking on eggshells)

524
00:22:17,446 --> 00:22:19,746
(The wasabi masterminds are sitting on edge.)

525
00:22:20,286 --> 00:22:22,956
(Meanwhile, the older sisters are completely at peace.)

526
00:22:22,956 --> 00:22:23,986
Squid and fishcake.

527
00:22:24,486 --> 00:22:25,756
It tastes amazing.

528
00:22:25,756 --> 00:22:26,886
(Stopping)

529
00:22:28,026 --> 00:22:29,196
Did you put mustard in it?

530
00:22:31,626 --> 00:22:33,896
(Startled)

531
00:22:34,066 --> 00:22:36,296
(A guilty look is written all over his face.)

532
00:22:39,006 --> 00:22:40,066
What?

533
00:22:40,066 --> 00:22:41,066
(What's the matter?)

534
00:22:41,066 --> 00:22:43,506
What?

535
00:22:43,506 --> 00:22:44,506
(Groaning)

536
00:22:46,006 --> 00:22:47,646
- Come here.
- Where's the wet tissue?

537
00:22:47,646 --> 00:22:48,976
- Was that your first bite?
- How did you eat that...

538
00:22:48,976 --> 00:22:50,316
as your first bite?

539
00:22:51,186 --> 00:22:53,946
(She makes a run for it.)

540
00:22:54,046 --> 00:22:55,116
(Screaming)

541
00:22:55,816 --> 00:22:58,556
(Soothing the shocked stomach with cold water)

542
00:22:58,826 --> 00:23:00,556
- I didn't see it coming so fast.
- On an empty stomach...

543
00:23:00,556 --> 00:23:01,626
I thought it'd take time.

544
00:23:01,626 --> 00:23:03,696
I was suspicious as soon as she grabbed it.

545
00:23:04,796 --> 00:23:05,896
(As soon as Jung Ah grabbed gimbap)

546
00:23:05,896 --> 00:23:07,726
(Frozen)

547
00:23:08,036 --> 00:23:10,366
(Realising what happened and suffering the burning pain instead)

548
00:23:10,366 --> 00:23:12,506
(He can't keep a straight face.)

549
00:23:12,836 --> 00:23:14,536
These guys are dangerous.

550
00:23:15,836 --> 00:23:16,976
- Was it a candid camera?
- Yes.

551
00:23:16,976 --> 00:23:18,976
How spicy is it? Give it to me.

552
00:23:18,976 --> 00:23:20,976
Let's see how spicy it is. I like mustard.

553
00:23:21,816 --> 00:23:23,216
You added a lot.

554
00:23:24,276 --> 00:23:25,886
This is no joke.

555
00:23:25,886 --> 00:23:27,956
I squeezed it out.

556
00:23:27,956 --> 00:23:28,986
I can't believe...

557
00:23:28,986 --> 00:23:30,616
- it was your first bite.
- You Seok, I thought...

558
00:23:30,616 --> 00:23:32,486
You added a line of wasabi in it?

559
00:23:32,486 --> 00:23:33,526
(The youngest siblings' surprise is a success.)

560
00:23:33,526 --> 00:23:35,456
(Giving a look)

561
00:23:35,726 --> 00:23:37,126
- Take them out now.
- There isn't anymore.

562
00:23:37,126 --> 00:23:38,466
- There isn't anymore.
- There was only one.

563
00:23:38,466 --> 00:23:39,866
- You're a lucky girl.
- You got picked.

564
00:23:40,596 --> 00:23:41,836
- Picked for what?
- That's so funny.

565
00:23:41,836 --> 00:23:43,096
You're picked as the deity of luck today.

566
00:23:43,096 --> 00:23:44,396
- The deity of luck?
- Yes.

567
00:23:44,396 --> 00:23:45,866
Your day will be full of good fortune today.

568
00:23:45,866 --> 00:23:48,206
(They start eating again with the deity of luck.)

569
00:23:49,176 --> 00:23:51,006
I thought, "Shall we wrap one with wasabi?"

570
00:23:51,006 --> 00:23:52,546
(Sun Young tries the seasoned squid and fishcake.)

571
00:23:52,706 --> 00:23:54,206
It tastes excellent.

572
00:23:55,516 --> 00:23:56,776
(A bite of the delicious seasoned dish...)

573
00:23:56,776 --> 00:23:59,086
(and a bite of gimbap)

574
00:23:59,386 --> 00:24:01,616
(When you eat the plain chungmu gimbap,)

575
00:24:02,686 --> 00:24:06,586
(you naturally crave the spicy seasoned squid and fishcake.)

576
00:24:06,586 --> 00:24:08,126
Jung Ah, it's very spicy.

577
00:24:08,256 --> 00:24:09,296
Right.

578
00:24:09,626 --> 00:24:11,826
(Doesn't it make it tastier?)

579
00:24:12,466 --> 00:24:13,866
- I can't stop eating it.
- I know.

580
00:24:15,936 --> 00:24:17,736
(Once you take a bite,)

581
00:24:17,736 --> 00:24:19,836
(you can't stop.)

582
00:24:20,266 --> 00:24:23,276
(The spicy flavour is addictive.)

583
00:24:23,276 --> 00:24:24,406
It's perfectly seasoned.

584
00:24:24,406 --> 00:24:26,806
(Jung Ah's seasoned squid and fishcake is deliciously spicy.)

585
00:24:26,806 --> 00:24:28,316
- It's so good.
- Jung Ah, it's really good.

586
00:24:28,316 --> 00:24:29,646
The seasoned fishcake is really good.

587
00:24:29,646 --> 00:24:30,746
Yes, it's very good.

588
00:24:30,746 --> 00:24:32,586
(Feeling proud)

589
00:24:32,786 --> 00:24:34,686
You can also make this at home.

590
00:24:35,686 --> 00:24:37,556
(We can make it too?)

591
00:24:37,556 --> 00:24:39,486
Jung Ah, did you add dried chilli in it?

592
00:24:39,726 --> 00:24:40,726
No, I didn't.

593
00:24:40,726 --> 00:24:42,026
- You didn't?
- No.

594
00:24:42,026 --> 00:24:45,026
Remember the Cheongyang chilli pepper you chopped for me?

595
00:24:45,026 --> 00:24:46,996
Right. And starch syrup.

596
00:24:46,996 --> 00:24:48,036
What else did you add?

597
00:24:48,036 --> 00:24:49,436
- Garlic.
- Garlic.

598
00:24:49,436 --> 00:24:50,696
- Chilli powder.
- Chilli powder

599
00:24:50,696 --> 00:24:51,806
Thick soy sauce.

600
00:24:51,806 --> 00:24:52,836
A bit of green plum syrup.

601
00:24:52,836 --> 00:24:54,106
Some ginger juice.

602
00:24:54,106 --> 00:24:55,776
You added ginger too?

603
00:24:56,076 --> 00:24:57,876
(Gosh, a lot goes in it.)

604
00:24:57,876 --> 00:24:59,376
You blanched squid and fishcake lightly.

605
00:24:59,376 --> 00:25:02,616
Yes, and I also added some sesame oil.

606
00:25:02,616 --> 00:25:03,876
- It takes a lot of work.
- It's done in no time.

607
00:25:04,116 --> 00:25:05,246
- You made it fast.
- Yes.

608
00:25:06,186 --> 00:25:07,686
She's like Bob Ross.

609
00:25:07,686 --> 00:25:09,456
You know the painter, Bob Ross?

610
00:25:09,456 --> 00:25:10,856
He says, "Isn't it easy?"

611
00:25:10,856 --> 00:25:12,156
- Right.
- You think, "Wait a minute."

612
00:25:12,256 --> 00:25:13,386
When you try it,

613
00:25:14,026 --> 00:25:15,226
you have no idea.

614
00:25:15,456 --> 00:25:16,496
You made it well too.

615
00:25:16,496 --> 00:25:17,696
And I think...

616
00:25:18,096 --> 00:25:20,826
- Yoon Seo studied fine arts.
- Right.

617
00:25:20,826 --> 00:25:22,596
- Me?
- You made the gimbap beautifully.

618
00:25:22,596 --> 00:25:24,296
- The gimbap?
- It turned out so pretty.

619
00:25:24,296 --> 00:25:26,306
People who majored in art have a special touch.

620
00:25:26,306 --> 00:25:27,836
Right. They're different.

621
00:25:27,836 --> 00:25:28,976
(The youngest is trapped in a cage of compliments.)

622
00:25:29,176 --> 00:25:31,406
- I made it with You Seok.
- It looks so pretty.

623
00:25:31,406 --> 00:25:32,406
(It's a work by Yoon Seo and You Seok.)

624
00:25:32,406 --> 00:25:34,576
Other than sesame oil, what did you add to the rice?

625
00:25:35,216 --> 00:25:36,876
- Did you add a bit of salt?
- A bit of seasoned salt.

626
00:25:37,946 --> 00:25:39,416
- Jung Ah told me...
- You added the perfect amount.

627
00:25:40,116 --> 00:25:41,556
- Good job.
- You did well.

628
00:25:41,556 --> 00:25:43,816
(With all the compliments, she can't hide her smile.)

629
00:25:43,916 --> 00:25:46,456
I have to try this. I've been dying to try it.

630
00:25:47,386 --> 00:25:49,356
What is it called? Pollack roe soup?

631
00:25:50,126 --> 00:25:53,026
I seasoned it with salted pollack roe and salted shrimp.

632
00:25:53,496 --> 00:25:56,896
(Sun Young and Yoon Seo try a sip at the same time.)

633
00:25:56,896 --> 00:25:58,036
It's good.

634
00:25:58,106 --> 00:25:59,806
(Humming)

635
00:26:00,166 --> 00:26:01,306
Isn't it light and clean?

636
00:26:01,306 --> 00:26:03,806
- This is why...
- It's very clean.

637
00:26:04,676 --> 00:26:09,046
(A clear broth that's light enough for breakfast)

638
00:26:13,386 --> 00:26:14,956
- The broth is amazing.
- Isn't it good?

639
00:26:18,656 --> 00:26:19,726
(Exhaling heavily)

640
00:26:21,026 --> 00:26:23,756
(Look at this guy.)

641
00:26:23,756 --> 00:26:25,396
The old man inside him is coming out again.

642
00:26:26,396 --> 00:26:28,736
(Tough Captain Kang whom they met yesterday)

643
00:26:29,066 --> 00:26:31,336
(He reappears today.)

644
00:26:31,406 --> 00:26:32,466
(Exhaling)

645
00:26:32,466 --> 00:26:33,506
(Moaning)

646
00:26:33,866 --> 00:26:35,306
(The reactions get more intense with every bite.)

647
00:26:35,306 --> 00:26:36,506
The broth is very nice.

648
00:26:39,106 --> 00:26:40,476
(The clean broth wins over the captain's palate.)

649
00:26:40,476 --> 00:26:42,416
It's easy and simple to make.

650
00:26:44,076 --> 00:26:45,386
It tastes much better than anything you buy.

651
00:26:45,386 --> 00:26:47,416
You use good ingredients when you make it at home.

652
00:26:47,416 --> 00:26:49,186
- I love this.
- Isn't it ripe?

653
00:26:50,216 --> 00:26:51,316
After just one day.

654
00:26:51,316 --> 00:26:54,356
(The radish and cabbage kimchi is aged perfectly after one day.)

655
00:26:56,256 --> 00:26:58,696
(Crunchy)

656
00:27:01,126 --> 00:27:03,236
(A satisfying crunch is an added bonus.)

657
00:27:03,866 --> 00:27:06,006
While lying here, I...

658
00:27:06,006 --> 00:27:07,806
(The refreshing radish and cabbage kimchi is...)

659
00:27:07,806 --> 00:27:09,576
(also the perfect match for chungmu gimbap.)

660
00:27:10,336 --> 00:27:15,376
(The breakfast tastes even better as it's shared.)

661
00:27:15,376 --> 00:27:16,946
Gosh. It's so good.

662
00:27:16,946 --> 00:27:17,946
(It tastes good too.)

663
00:27:17,946 --> 00:27:18,986
It's really good.

664
00:27:19,786 --> 00:27:21,246
- The weather is so nice.
- Right?

665
00:27:22,286 --> 00:27:24,786
(It's the perfect beginning of the day.)

666
00:27:25,986 --> 00:27:27,526
What kind of work are we going to do today?

667
00:27:27,756 --> 00:27:29,096
- Will you tell us now?
- Where will we go?

668
00:27:29,596 --> 00:27:31,196
- You'll know when you get there.
- Really?

669
00:27:31,196 --> 00:27:32,866
- You won't tell us until then?
- They won't tell us.

670
00:27:33,766 --> 00:27:35,436
- I thought we'd find out by now.
- They won't tell us even now?

671
00:27:35,436 --> 00:27:36,496
(The youngest members are anxious.)

672
00:27:36,696 --> 00:27:38,136
What's the point of finding out now?

673
00:27:38,136 --> 00:27:40,766
We'll find out when we get there after a 20-minute drive.

674
00:27:40,766 --> 00:27:41,876
I need to prepare myself emotionally.

675
00:27:42,206 --> 00:27:43,436
- Gosh, I'm so full.
- I didn't know this was here.

676
00:27:45,206 --> 00:27:47,106
You said we'd leave at 11am, right?

677
00:27:47,106 --> 00:27:48,416
- What time is it now?
- It's 10am.

678
00:27:48,716 --> 00:27:50,416
Let's catch a quick 30-minute nap.

679
00:27:50,816 --> 00:27:51,846
Go ahead and take a nap.

680
00:27:51,846 --> 00:27:53,446
The food coma must've kicked in.

681
00:27:53,446 --> 00:27:55,356
Right. My blood sugar spike just kicked in.

682
00:27:55,356 --> 00:27:56,956
- Right. Go ahead and take a nap.
- Okay.

683
00:27:57,386 --> 00:27:59,286
Time to split up, you guys.

684
00:27:59,686 --> 00:28:00,726
- But hold on...
- We're still...

685
00:28:00,726 --> 00:28:01,796
- You'll talk without me.
- We're still eating.

686
00:28:01,796 --> 00:28:02,796
Give us a second, Sun Young.

687
00:28:02,796 --> 00:28:04,256
Go on and take a nap. We'll be talking about interesting stuff.

688
00:28:04,256 --> 00:28:05,326
- No.
- You can keep the door open.

689
00:28:05,326 --> 00:28:06,396
Keep the door open so you can hear us.

690
00:28:06,396 --> 00:28:08,596
- Keep it open like last night.
- You heard us last night.

691
00:28:08,896 --> 00:28:11,366
(Should I take a nap or not?)

692
00:28:11,706 --> 00:28:13,236
- Seriously.
- She left the door open...

693
00:28:13,236 --> 00:28:15,376
- not to miss anything.
- She heard everything.

694
00:28:15,676 --> 00:28:16,936
She heard almost everything before she fell asleep.

695
00:28:16,936 --> 00:28:18,546
(Don't have fun without me.)

696
00:28:18,546 --> 00:28:20,746
- I thought there was no camera.
- It was fun.

697
00:28:20,946 --> 00:28:21,976
It was so funny.

698
00:28:22,216 --> 00:28:24,446
Nobody has ever kept talking to me like you guys did.

699
00:28:25,246 --> 00:28:27,116
Yoon Seo and I went outside to stargaze last night.

700
00:28:27,386 --> 00:28:28,486
- Did you?
- Yes.

701
00:28:28,486 --> 00:28:29,886
- Wasn't it like a drama?
- It was.

702
00:28:30,016 --> 00:28:32,056
Right? I felt like we were at a place like...

703
00:28:32,386 --> 00:28:35,496
The Big Dipper was clearly visible. It was really nice.

704
00:28:35,956 --> 00:28:37,496
Didn't you...

705
00:28:37,626 --> 00:28:39,396
feel a spark or something romantic?

706
00:28:39,396 --> 00:28:40,626
(Shaking his head)

707
00:28:40,626 --> 00:28:41,836
- You were alone with her.
- We just...

708
00:28:42,236 --> 00:28:44,396
enjoyed watching the sea and the sky.

709
00:28:44,396 --> 00:28:45,436
Sorry to disappoint you.

710
00:28:45,436 --> 00:28:46,806
- Sorry.
- You didn't feel a thing?

711
00:28:46,806 --> 00:28:47,836
No.

712
00:28:48,476 --> 00:28:50,476
- But it was really nice, right?
- Yes, it was really nice.

713
00:28:50,936 --> 00:28:52,206
You two are like close siblings.

714
00:28:52,206 --> 00:28:53,276
(She seems a bit disappointed. "I see. You two are like siblings.")

715
00:28:53,606 --> 00:28:55,576
Let's warm up a bit before we head out.

716
00:28:55,576 --> 00:28:56,576
- Okay.
- Okay.

717
00:28:56,646 --> 00:28:59,916
Let's play rock-paper-scissors...

718
00:28:59,916 --> 00:29:01,616
to choose today's instructor.

719
00:29:02,086 --> 00:29:04,756
(Winking?)

720
00:29:05,086 --> 00:29:06,086
(Chuckling)

721
00:29:06,086 --> 00:29:07,726
- Sounds good.
- Sounds good.

722
00:29:07,726 --> 00:29:09,496
(Grinning)

723
00:29:10,056 --> 00:29:11,526
(They give off a subtle suspicious vibe.)

724
00:29:11,526 --> 00:29:12,566
Sounds good.

725
00:29:13,326 --> 00:29:16,636
(Earlier, while Sun Young was gone...)

726
00:29:17,136 --> 00:29:19,136
Didn't we plan to exercise today?

727
00:29:19,136 --> 00:29:20,636
- Feel free to use it.
- Right before we head out.

728
00:29:20,636 --> 00:29:21,776
Who will be the instructor?

729
00:29:21,776 --> 00:29:22,806
- Let's play rock-paper-scissors.
- Yesterday...

730
00:29:22,806 --> 00:29:23,976
Let's play rock-paper-scissors.

731
00:29:24,076 --> 00:29:25,206
But let's rig the results.

732
00:29:25,206 --> 00:29:26,206
How?

733
00:29:26,206 --> 00:29:27,806
We'll throw rock, then scissors, and then paper.

734
00:29:28,006 --> 00:29:29,576
- Rock, scissors, and then paper?
- Rock, scissors, and then paper.

735
00:29:29,676 --> 00:29:30,976
- So... Rock-paper-scissors.
- Rock-paper-scissors.

736
00:29:30,976 --> 00:29:32,386
(They came up with a little plot, led by the playful You Seok.)

737
00:29:32,386 --> 00:29:33,486
It'll be decided within three rounds.

738
00:29:33,716 --> 00:29:35,016
Are you sure we should play rock-paper-scissors?

739
00:29:35,356 --> 00:29:36,616
- Yes!
- I'm a pro at that game.

740
00:29:36,616 --> 00:29:37,886
Sun Young, are you good at rock-paper-scissors?

741
00:29:38,656 --> 00:29:40,156
- No.
- Are you bad at it?

742
00:29:40,156 --> 00:29:41,186
Yes.

743
00:29:41,186 --> 00:29:42,256
(You'll end up in last place anyway.)

744
00:29:42,256 --> 00:29:43,296
Are you?

745
00:29:43,296 --> 00:29:44,356
The four of us will play the game.

746
00:29:44,356 --> 00:29:46,296
- The loser will be the instructor.
- Okay.

747
00:29:46,396 --> 00:29:48,236
- Here we go.
- Ready or not,

748
00:29:48,236 --> 00:29:49,466
- rock-paper-scissors.
- Rock-paper-scissors.

749
00:29:49,466 --> 00:29:51,366
(Rock, rock, paper, rock)

750
00:29:52,006 --> 00:29:53,036
Oh, yes.

751
00:29:54,066 --> 00:29:56,276
(We didn't expect this.)

752
00:29:56,636 --> 00:29:58,406
- From now on, it's war.
- You little...

753
00:29:58,406 --> 00:29:59,446
From now on, it's war.

754
00:29:59,446 --> 00:30:01,276
(Come over here, you punk.)

755
00:30:01,276 --> 00:30:03,216
(Quiet down! We might get caught.)

756
00:30:03,416 --> 00:30:05,116
- Why? What are you going to do?
- We'll play rock-paper-scissors.

757
00:30:05,116 --> 00:30:06,116
Okay.

758
00:30:06,116 --> 00:30:07,346
- Go ahead. Ready.
- Ready or not,

759
00:30:07,346 --> 00:30:08,456
rock-paper-scissors.

760
00:30:08,456 --> 00:30:10,486
(Scissors, rock, scissors)

761
00:30:11,186 --> 00:30:12,686
- I'm not the one either.
- You aren't?

762
00:30:13,426 --> 00:30:15,396
- Seriously.
- What? I said it was war.

763
00:30:16,056 --> 00:30:17,926
He's the one who started this. Let's do it.

764
00:30:18,326 --> 00:30:19,626
Rock-paper-scissors.

765
00:30:19,666 --> 00:30:21,396
(Yoon Seo wins.)

766
00:30:21,396 --> 00:30:22,466
We'll follow our instructor's lead.

767
00:30:22,466 --> 00:30:24,136
- Follow my lead.
- Got it.

768
00:30:24,136 --> 00:30:25,866
Please show us some good exercises for the back.

