1012
00:40:04,976 --> 00:40:09,086
(This pole has been designated as a national heritage. It's called...)

1013
00:40:10,286 --> 00:40:13,026
(Teulitdae)

1014
00:40:13,956 --> 00:40:17,456
(It's designed to be long to harvest seaweed from the deep sea floor.)

1015
00:40:17,656 --> 00:40:19,296
If you push it deep into the water,

1016
00:40:19,296 --> 00:40:21,526
(When you push the teulitdae all the way down to the bottom...)

1017
00:40:21,596 --> 00:40:24,636
it reaches the seaweed at the bottom.

1018
00:40:25,396 --> 00:40:28,436
The tip just reached the bottom, in the middle of the seaweed.

1019
00:40:28,436 --> 00:40:29,806
(The teulitdae has settled right into the seaweed forest.)

1020
00:40:30,206 --> 00:40:33,476
Next, you spin the handle. And then the seaweed...

1021
00:40:33,476 --> 00:40:34,546
(Spin the handle with the teulitdae firmly on the bottom.)

1022
00:40:35,006 --> 00:40:36,816
If there's seaweed down there, it'll coil around the teulitdae.

1023
00:40:36,816 --> 00:40:38,176
(The seaweed coils tightly around the teulitdae.)

1024
00:40:39,546 --> 00:40:40,616
After spinning the handle a few times...

1025
00:40:40,616 --> 00:40:42,186
(When there's enough seaweed coiled around the teulitdae...)

1026
00:40:43,756 --> 00:40:45,216
You pull it out when the seaweed is wrapped around the teulitdae.

1027
00:40:45,216 --> 00:40:46,456
(It's time to pull it out of the water.)

1028
00:40:47,086 --> 00:40:51,596
(The seaweed emerges from the water, wrapped around the teulitdae.)

1029
00:40:53,226 --> 00:40:55,126
(It's so easy, isn't it?)

1030
00:40:55,696 --> 00:40:57,266
- That's amazing.
- Right.

1031
00:40:58,266 --> 00:41:00,766
(The added weight of the seaweed makes it twice as heavy.)

1032
00:41:01,506 --> 00:41:02,536
(Lastly, you shake the seaweed off the teulitdae, and that's it.)

1033
00:41:02,536 --> 00:41:03,936
- This is how it's done.
- I see.

1034
00:41:04,476 --> 00:41:07,376
- This is how you harvest seaweed.
- Yes.

1035
00:41:07,376 --> 00:41:08,376
(It weighs about 30kg to 40kg. This work takes immense expertise.)

1036
00:41:08,746 --> 00:41:10,216
Do you want to try it?

1037
00:41:10,516 --> 00:41:12,486
- Yes. It looks very heavy.
- It's heavy.

1038
00:41:12,486 --> 00:41:13,546
(Will the older members do it well?)

1039
00:41:13,746 --> 00:41:15,416
- Try to put it into the water.
- Got it.

1040
00:41:17,856 --> 00:41:18,926
Here we go.

1041
00:41:18,926 --> 00:41:21,526
(As soon as they lift it up, they can feel the massive weight.)

1042
00:41:22,156 --> 00:41:24,056
(It's still too heavy for even two people to lift easily.)

1043
00:41:24,056 --> 00:41:26,366
(Gasping)

1044
00:41:27,196 --> 00:41:29,596
He said we should keep it close to the boat.

1045
00:41:30,596 --> 00:41:31,936
- First...
- Move it toward the bow.

1046
00:41:31,936 --> 00:41:33,866
- Toward the bow.
- Got it. Let's lift it again.

1047
00:41:34,606 --> 00:41:35,636
Toward the bow... Gosh.

1048
00:41:39,806 --> 00:41:40,906
I'll move to this side, Jung Ah.

1049
00:41:40,906 --> 00:41:44,546
(Just lifting it up and putting it in the water is already a struggle.)

1050
00:41:45,646 --> 00:41:47,286
- Step over to this side.
- Got it.

1051
00:41:47,286 --> 00:41:48,346
(They're being dragged by the teulitdae just like seaweed.)

1052
00:41:48,346 --> 00:41:49,356
All right. Let's do it this way.

1053
00:41:49,556 --> 00:41:51,486
- Okay. All right.
- Now, push it into the water.

1054
00:41:52,186 --> 00:41:54,986
- Plunge it quickly.
- Pushing it... Let's do it quickly.

1055
00:41:55,486 --> 00:41:57,326
- As quickly as possible.
- Right.

1056
00:41:57,896 --> 00:41:59,966
- It should be locked into place.
- Keep pushing it.

1057
00:41:59,966 --> 00:42:01,666
(They barely managed to get it into the water.)

1058
00:42:02,866 --> 00:42:06,336
(But the teulitdae keeps floating back up because of buoyancy.)

1059
00:42:07,506 --> 00:42:10,906
(It's almost at the bottom, but it's still fighting back.)

1060
00:42:11,606 --> 00:42:13,806
Push it all the way down until it reaches the bottom.

1061
00:42:13,806 --> 00:42:14,876
(Floating back up)

1062
00:42:15,246 --> 00:42:16,646
It will strike the bottom if you plunge it quickly.

1063
00:42:16,746 --> 00:42:18,776
- It won't reach the bottom.
- Wait until it's all the way down.

1064
00:42:18,776 --> 00:42:19,816
It'll strike the bottom when it's all the way down?

1065
00:42:20,416 --> 00:42:21,446
(Grunting)

1066
00:42:21,446 --> 00:42:22,686
(Chuckling)

1067
00:42:22,686 --> 00:42:23,916
(Floating back up)

1068
00:42:24,556 --> 00:42:26,486
At this rate, you won't even get enough seaweed to make a side dish.

1069
00:42:26,486 --> 00:42:28,056
That's not true. We can do this.

1070
00:42:30,256 --> 00:42:31,596
- It just hit the bottom.
- It hit the bottom.

1071
00:42:32,056 --> 00:42:33,066
- We should spin the handle now.
- Now, spin the handle.

1072
00:42:33,066 --> 00:42:34,066
(Finally, it seems like the teulitdae hit the bottom.)

1073
00:42:34,066 --> 00:42:35,836
- Spin it.
- I'll do it.

1074
00:42:36,396 --> 00:42:38,096
I think spinning the handle is easier. I'll hold the pole.

1075
00:42:38,696 --> 00:42:39,736
Jung Ah, you spin it.

1076
00:42:39,836 --> 00:42:41,366
It's hard to hold the pole. Goodness.

1077
00:42:41,366 --> 00:42:42,376
(Goodness)

1078
00:42:45,336 --> 00:42:46,976
(Oh, no)

1079
00:42:47,346 --> 00:42:49,976
(She might get hurt while trying to harvest seaweed.)

1080
00:42:51,346 --> 00:42:54,286
Spinning it will feel different once the seaweed wraps around.

1081
00:42:54,716 --> 00:42:55,986
- You can feel that?
- Yes.

1082
00:42:55,986 --> 00:42:58,156
- It becomes heavy.
- I see.

1083
00:42:58,156 --> 00:42:59,586
Hold on. I can feel its weight...

1084
00:42:59,586 --> 00:43:01,026
- when it wraps around?
- That's right.

1085
00:43:03,256 --> 00:43:06,226
(Does it mean the teulitdae is...)

1086
00:43:06,526 --> 00:43:07,596
It's not at the bottom, is it?

1087
00:43:08,496 --> 00:43:10,266
It should strike the bottom.

1088
00:43:10,636 --> 00:43:11,766
It should be at the bottom.

1089
00:43:11,766 --> 00:43:12,966
(It's spinning around without settling on the bottom.)

1090
00:43:12,966 --> 00:43:13,966
It should be at the bottom.

1091
00:43:13,966 --> 00:43:15,166
(It's spinning around without settling on the bottom.)

1092
00:43:15,736 --> 00:43:16,776
It should be at the bottom.

1093
00:43:16,776 --> 00:43:18,806
- It hit the bottom.
- Right. Spin the handle.

1094
00:43:18,806 --> 00:43:19,806
Okay. I'll spin it.

1095
00:43:19,806 --> 00:43:21,806
(Will they be able to harvest any seaweed by the end of the day?)

1096
00:43:22,546 --> 00:43:23,616
Gosh.

1097
00:43:23,616 --> 00:43:25,146
(Grunting)

1098
00:43:27,346 --> 00:43:29,586
- You're so bad at this.
- Jung Ah, can you move aside?

1099
00:43:29,586 --> 00:43:30,916
You wouldn't survive on Geoje Island.

1100
00:43:32,626 --> 00:43:35,956
(Even so, they keep spinning it with every ounce of their strength.)

1101
00:43:36,956 --> 00:43:39,496
- Because this is so heavy...
- Hold on a second.

1102
00:43:39,496 --> 00:43:40,796
Oh, my. We got it.

1103
00:43:41,466 --> 00:43:42,536
Awesome.

1104
00:43:42,536 --> 00:43:45,296
(As they spun the handle, the teulitdae became heavier.)

1105
00:43:46,006 --> 00:43:47,006
Pull it out now.

1106
00:43:48,236 --> 00:43:49,336
Let's see if you can survive on Geoje Island.

1107
00:43:50,476 --> 00:43:51,606
(Gulping)

1108
00:43:52,176 --> 00:43:54,476
(Combining their strength, they pull it out slowly.)

1109
00:43:55,576 --> 00:43:57,316
Oh, we got a little.

1110
00:43:58,676 --> 00:43:59,986
Sir, we got a little bit of seaweed.

1111
00:43:59,986 --> 00:44:01,186
(It's not a lot, but they succeeded in getting it out of the water.)

1112
00:44:01,886 --> 00:44:04,286
- Let's bring it safe on board.
- In the opposite direction...

1113
00:44:04,286 --> 00:44:05,356
- Check this out.
- Okay.

1114
00:44:06,686 --> 00:44:08,256
Why is there a rock stuck to the seaweed?

1115
00:44:09,026 --> 00:44:12,296
(Because it's wild "rock" seaweed.)

1116
00:44:12,696 --> 00:44:14,066
- This is called wild rock seaweed.
- Yes.

1117
00:44:14,066 --> 00:44:15,396
- It's organic.
- I see.

1118
00:44:15,396 --> 00:44:18,396
- It grows on rocks.
- Oh, I see. It grows on rocks.

1119
00:44:18,666 --> 00:44:19,966
There are rocks everywhere down there.

1120
00:44:20,436 --> 00:44:22,006
- So it's attached to rocks?
- Yes.

1121
00:44:22,006 --> 00:44:23,476
(That's why a rock tags along sometimes.)

1122
00:44:24,376 --> 00:44:25,376
Now we need to...

1123
00:44:27,046 --> 00:44:29,976
(Carefully separate the seaweed from the teulitdae.)

1124
00:44:33,216 --> 00:44:35,286
- Cut it and toss the rock.
- Okay.

1125
00:44:35,386 --> 00:44:39,356
(And that's how you harvest the top-quality wild rock seaweed.)

1126
00:44:41,356 --> 00:44:44,196
Hold on. You throw out this part, right? Do you eat this part too?

1127
00:44:44,796 --> 00:44:46,026
We eat that seaweed sporophyll.

1128
00:44:46,026 --> 00:44:47,196
- Oh, I see.
- Seaweed sporophyll.

1129
00:44:48,196 --> 00:44:49,196
I like seaweed sporophyll.

1130
00:44:49,196 --> 00:44:50,636
(You can only harvest it only when it comes out with a rock.)

1131
00:44:50,866 --> 00:44:52,636
This must be the finest product, right?

1132
00:44:52,636 --> 00:44:53,706
(They even got seaweed sporophyll, which is very rare, from the start.)

1133
00:44:53,806 --> 00:44:55,136
I really love seaweed.

1134
00:44:58,036 --> 00:45:00,446
(Sniffing)

1135
00:45:01,306 --> 00:45:04,716
(While the older members are lost in the joy of their first harvest...)

1136
00:45:05,116 --> 00:45:06,416
When the seaweed wraps around,

1137
00:45:06,416 --> 00:45:07,686
- Yes.
- it gets harder to spin the handle.

1138
00:45:07,686 --> 00:45:09,386
(Meanwhile, the youngest members are still learning how to do it.)

1139
00:45:09,986 --> 00:45:13,056
- It's really hard for a beginner.
- For a beginner.

1140
00:45:14,586 --> 00:45:17,496
Spin the handle a few times and pull it up when you get seaweed.

1141
00:45:18,626 --> 00:45:20,366
- Oh, my. Look at that.
- And you get seaweed...

1142
00:45:20,696 --> 00:45:22,266
- You get seaweed like this.
- That's amazing.

1143
00:45:22,266 --> 00:45:24,236
This is considered a small amount.

1144
00:45:24,236 --> 00:45:25,766
- Is this a small amount?
- Once you pull it on board,

1145
00:45:25,766 --> 00:45:27,306
you can untangle it from the teulitdae.

1146
00:45:27,306 --> 00:45:28,466
Just put it on top of the seaweed.

1147
00:45:29,176 --> 00:45:30,806
So this is wild rock seaweed.

1148
00:45:30,806 --> 00:45:32,376
Yes, this is wild rock seaweed.

1149
00:45:33,276 --> 00:45:35,846
- We're filling the boat with this.
- That'd be great.

1150
00:45:36,816 --> 00:45:39,516
(They've learned everything. Captain Kang steps up bravely.)

1151
00:45:40,246 --> 00:45:42,886
(I drove a boat yesterday. This is nothing.)

1152
00:45:42,886 --> 00:45:44,086
(Let's fill the boat with seaweed.)

1153
00:45:45,486 --> 00:45:47,986
(He's full of confidence.)

1154
00:45:48,156 --> 00:45:51,226
You have to plunge it vertically along the current.

1155
00:45:51,226 --> 00:45:53,766
(He quickly plunges the heavy teulitdae into the water.)

1156
00:45:54,996 --> 00:45:56,496
It's at the bottom now. Try to spin the handle.

1157
00:45:57,596 --> 00:45:59,736
(Now he has to spin the handle to get the seaweed to wrap around.)

1158
00:46:00,536 --> 00:46:02,066
Hold this part... That's good. Now, try to spin it.

1159
00:46:02,266 --> 00:46:03,336
(Squeaking)

1160
00:46:05,467 --> 00:46:07,467
(How well will Captain Kang do?)

1161
00:46:07,607 --> 00:46:08,607
(Squeaking)

1162
00:46:10,477 --> 00:46:11,477
(Squeaking)

1163
00:46:11,477 --> 00:46:13,707
(The handle doesn't spin easily.)

1164
00:46:14,107 --> 00:46:15,907
Try to spin it. Keep trying.

1165
00:46:17,017 --> 00:46:18,947
- Is it heavy?
- There's a rock.

1166
00:46:18,994 --> 00:46:20,700
In that case, shake it off.

1167
00:46:21,951 --> 00:46:24,521
Captain did it so easily, but you look...

1168
00:46:24,961 --> 00:46:28,031
(Looking quite different from the bold start)

1169
00:46:28,931 --> 00:46:30,701
Captain spun it so easily before.

1170
00:46:30,931 --> 00:46:34,201
(Captain Kang's pride has taken a hit.)

1171
00:46:35,001 --> 00:46:37,001
(Frowning)

1172
00:46:37,001 --> 00:46:39,201
(Laughing)

1173
00:46:40,171 --> 00:46:41,171
Gosh, it's...

1174
00:46:41,811 --> 00:46:45,741
It's not easy to spin it. It requires strength.

1175
00:46:45,741 --> 00:46:48,011
(You Seok, Captain)

1176
00:46:49,081 --> 00:46:50,351
- He's laughing.
- What if I harvest nothing?

1177
00:46:51,551 --> 00:46:52,551
(Psyching up)

1178
00:46:53,691 --> 00:46:55,591
The pole has caught between rocks.

1179
00:46:55,751 --> 00:46:56,821
(Exclaiming)

1180
00:46:56,821 --> 00:46:58,261
(Using every ounce of his strength)

1181
00:46:58,991 --> 00:47:01,261
Gosh. It requires lots of strength.

1182
00:47:02,491 --> 00:47:04,201
- I told you that it was tough.
- Come on.

1183
00:47:04,201 --> 00:47:06,061
You made it look so easy.

1184
00:47:06,061 --> 00:47:07,071
You did it so easily.

1185
00:47:07,071 --> 00:47:08,631
So, I thought it'd be easy.

1186
00:47:08,631 --> 00:47:09,701
Right.

1187
00:47:10,701 --> 00:47:12,201
If it doesn't spin, just take it out.

1188
00:47:12,641 --> 00:47:13,871
Pull it up. Yes.

1189
00:47:15,971 --> 00:47:19,041
(They decided to pull it up, instead of keep spinning it.)

1190
00:47:19,651 --> 00:47:21,111
Gosh. It's really heavy.

1191
00:47:22,981 --> 00:47:24,121
(He takes it out with Yoon Seo's help.)

1192
00:47:24,121 --> 00:47:25,251
Gosh. It's heavy.

1193
00:47:26,721 --> 00:47:27,851
(Surprised)

1194
00:47:27,851 --> 00:47:29,351
(Shocked)

1195
00:47:29,391 --> 00:47:30,791
Is this all I managed to harvest?

1196
00:47:32,561 --> 00:47:35,561
(A bit underwhelming)

1197
00:47:35,931 --> 00:47:38,361
At this rate, you won't make a living.

1198
00:47:38,361 --> 00:47:39,431
You won't make a living.

1199
00:47:39,971 --> 00:47:41,571
No one will feed him, if that's all he can do.

1200
00:47:42,471 --> 00:47:43,571
- They won't feed you.
- No.

1201
00:47:43,571 --> 00:47:44,601
(Joking)

1202
00:47:44,601 --> 00:47:46,371
You should have harvested more.

1203
00:47:46,371 --> 00:47:50,641
(Captain Kang's back looks dejected.)

1204
00:47:51,111 --> 00:47:52,741
We have to hurry and harvest more.

1205
00:47:54,951 --> 00:47:56,721
(Passing)

1206
00:47:56,721 --> 00:47:57,781
Okay. Try it.

1207
00:47:57,781 --> 00:47:59,691
(Yoon Seo takes over the pole right away.)

1208
00:47:59,691 --> 00:48:00,791
Diagonally.

1209
00:48:00,791 --> 00:48:02,721
- Pull it more.
- You have to pull it more.

1210
00:48:02,721 --> 00:48:04,091
- Pull it more.
- Pull it.

1211
00:48:04,761 --> 00:48:06,861
- Now, stick it in.
- Let it go, and it'll go in.

1212
00:48:06,861 --> 00:48:09,061
At first, just stick it in.

1213
00:48:09,061 --> 00:48:11,161
When you stick it in, it goes downward automatically.

1214
00:48:11,161 --> 00:48:12,361
(She confidently raised the pole and plunged it into the sea.)

1215
00:48:15,501 --> 00:48:18,101
It has reached the seaweed bed.

1216
00:48:18,101 --> 00:48:19,301
(It easily reached the seaweed bed.)

1217
00:48:19,841 --> 00:48:20,841
(Screaming)

1218
00:48:20,841 --> 00:48:22,311
It spins easily.

1219
00:48:23,481 --> 00:48:25,211
It rotates easily.

1220
00:48:25,211 --> 00:48:26,581
(Unlike Captain Kang, she spins it easily.)

1221
00:48:26,811 --> 00:48:28,381
If it turns easily, it means there is no seaweed.

1222
00:48:28,381 --> 00:48:29,381
Pardon?

1223
00:48:30,351 --> 00:48:31,681
- Really?
- It means there's nothing.

1224
00:48:32,781 --> 00:48:37,921
(Actually, the pole turned easily because there was less seaweed.)

1225
00:48:38,461 --> 00:48:40,591
We can't go home until we fill up the boat, can we?

1226
00:48:40,591 --> 00:48:42,461
No. You won't be going home.

1227
00:48:43,561 --> 00:48:45,361
Hey, I don't think we'll make it home today.

1228
00:48:45,361 --> 00:48:46,931
You won't go back home today.

1229
00:48:48,171 --> 00:48:49,871
- Bring it here.
- It spins so well.

1230
00:48:49,901 --> 00:48:51,141
- Bring it over here.
- Really?

1231
00:48:53,571 --> 00:48:54,871
(Laughing)

1232
00:48:55,841 --> 00:48:59,011
(Finding seaweed isn't easy either.)

1233
00:48:59,241 --> 00:49:00,581
Go further back.

1234
00:49:00,581 --> 00:49:01,611
- I need to go back.
- Yes.

1235
00:49:02,651 --> 00:49:03,651
(Screaming)

1236
00:49:04,781 --> 00:49:05,981
Did it catch on something?

1237
00:49:07,391 --> 00:49:10,491
(It instantly becomes harder to spin when there is more seaweed.)

1238
00:49:10,491 --> 00:49:11,491
Hold on.

1239
00:49:12,791 --> 00:49:16,131
(It gets stuck right away.)

1240
00:49:16,961 --> 00:49:18,001
Gosh, this is...

1241
00:49:18,261 --> 00:49:19,601
Hold on. What about Jung Ah and Sun Young?

1242
00:49:20,831 --> 00:49:21,831
Hold on.

1243
00:49:21,831 --> 00:49:23,441
(Doing her best while worrying about the older members)

1244
00:49:24,171 --> 00:49:25,641
(Grunting)

1245
00:49:26,101 --> 00:49:27,341
(Groaning)

1246
00:49:28,271 --> 00:49:29,881
Gosh. You're quite the worker.

1247
00:49:29,881 --> 00:49:30,911
(Proud)

1248
00:49:30,911 --> 00:49:32,181
I'm struggling.

1249
00:49:32,181 --> 00:49:33,981
How could I be the worker when I'm struggling so much?

1250
00:49:33,981 --> 00:49:35,051
(Embarrassed)

1251
00:49:36,751 --> 00:49:37,981
This is so hard.

1252
00:49:38,221 --> 00:49:40,421
(While saying it's hard, she suddenly spins it fast.)

1253
00:49:40,821 --> 00:49:42,421
(Fully determined)

1254
00:49:43,161 --> 00:49:44,161
(Groaning)

1255
00:49:44,161 --> 00:49:46,691
(She spins the pole with grit and determination.)

1256
00:49:47,261 --> 00:49:48,331
(Grunting)

1257
00:49:48,331 --> 00:49:50,401
(She keeps rotating it with all her effort.)

1258
00:49:50,701 --> 00:49:52,001
It's spinning.

1259
00:49:55,071 --> 00:49:58,871
(In the end, she even goes crazy.)

1260
00:49:59,471 --> 00:50:00,711
(Amazed)

1261
00:50:00,711 --> 00:50:02,211
It wraps the seaweed around the pole now.

1262
00:50:02,771 --> 00:50:05,881
(Spinning at a whole different speed than Captain Kang)

1263
00:50:07,681 --> 00:50:10,821
(Tough Yoon Seo)

1264
00:50:10,981 --> 00:50:12,621
Okay. Try pulling it up now.

1265
00:50:13,951 --> 00:50:15,721
Gosh. It's heavy.

1266
00:50:17,161 --> 00:50:18,161
It's okay.

1267
00:50:19,191 --> 00:50:22,131
(She retracts the pole confidently by herself.)

1268
00:50:22,561 --> 00:50:23,601
It's coming.

1269
00:50:23,601 --> 00:50:24,701
(Surprised)

1270
00:50:24,701 --> 00:50:25,831
(Surprised)

1271
00:50:28,801 --> 00:50:30,141
Gosh. You're good at this.

1272
00:50:31,401 --> 00:50:33,271
(Jackpot!)

1273
00:50:33,371 --> 00:50:34,941
It's a lot. Do I shake it off?

1274
00:50:38,741 --> 00:50:40,411
You got more than I did.

1275
00:50:41,851 --> 00:50:43,011
You're a natural.

1276
00:50:44,121 --> 00:50:46,591
Captain, I'll come work here if I can't stay in Seoul.

1277
00:50:46,591 --> 00:50:47,821
(Yoon Seo finally found her calling.)

1278
00:50:49,051 --> 00:50:50,361
- You're good.
- Yes, she's good.

1279
00:50:50,361 --> 00:50:52,021
- Is it not bad?
- She's a great worker.

1280
00:50:52,091 --> 00:50:53,261
Try it again.

1281
00:50:53,561 --> 00:50:55,291
- I'll try it again.
- Will you?

1282
00:50:55,931 --> 00:50:57,261
I'll do it. Take some rest.

1283
00:50:57,301 --> 00:50:58,931
- Should we take turns?
- Yes.

1284
00:50:58,931 --> 00:51:00,101
- Plunge it.
- Throw it.

1285
00:51:00,101 --> 00:51:01,171
(Captain Kang tries it again, provoked by Yoon Seo.)

1286
00:51:01,171 --> 00:51:02,271
Reach the bed.

1287
00:51:03,271 --> 00:51:04,541
- Then turn it.
- Place the pole.

1288
00:51:04,541 --> 00:51:05,671
- Spin it more.
- Then I spin it.

1289
00:51:06,341 --> 00:51:07,711
(Surprised)

1290
00:51:08,311 --> 00:51:10,611
It has gotten easier for you. But as soon as I said that,

1291
00:51:11,541 --> 00:51:12,541
it has become tough.

1292
00:51:13,181 --> 00:51:14,381
If it doesn't turn at all, pull it up.

1293
00:51:14,381 --> 00:51:15,811
You can pull it up and try it again.

1294
00:51:15,811 --> 00:51:17,781
If there is only the head of the seaweed, it doesn't turn.

1295
00:51:17,951 --> 00:51:19,021
(Grunting)

1296
00:51:19,451 --> 00:51:20,451
Are you okay?

1297
00:51:20,451 --> 00:51:21,821
(Laughing)

1298
00:51:22,491 --> 00:51:23,621
(Groaning)

1299
00:51:23,621 --> 00:51:26,321
(You Seok only lets out weak little grunts.)

1300
00:51:26,761 --> 00:51:27,931
The current is too strong.

1301
00:51:28,991 --> 00:51:30,001
(Grunting)

1302
00:51:30,001 --> 00:51:32,661
(While the younger siblings do their best to harvest seaweed,)

1303
00:51:33,131 --> 00:51:34,931
Gosh. Turn it.

1304
00:51:34,931 --> 00:51:37,701
(the older siblings are going all in with the harvest too.)

1305
00:51:38,001 --> 00:51:39,271
Jung Ah, I'll turn it.

1306
00:51:39,271 --> 00:51:40,971
- You do it.
- I'll do it.

1307
00:51:41,141 --> 00:51:42,841
- Hold the pole.
- You spin it.

1308
00:51:42,841 --> 00:51:45,181
(The two of them work on it harmoniously.)

1309
00:51:45,581 --> 00:51:46,681
You shouldn't hold it like that.

1310
00:51:46,811 --> 00:51:48,411
You have to hold this part to spin it.

1311
00:51:48,981 --> 00:51:50,081
Okay.

1312
00:51:51,421 --> 00:51:52,551
Let's try it again.

1313
00:51:52,781 --> 00:51:54,521
- We caught some.
- Gosh.

1314
00:51:55,291 --> 00:51:56,391
(Grunting)

1315
00:51:57,561 --> 00:51:59,391
(Losing their sanity)

1316
00:51:59,391 --> 00:52:01,531
I'm giving birth right now.

1317
00:52:01,531 --> 00:52:03,331
- Gosh. Oh, dear.
- Gosh.

1318
00:52:03,331 --> 00:52:04,501
I've already given birth to two.

1319
00:52:05,431 --> 00:52:09,771
(While working, they understood what going all in feels like.)

1320
00:52:10,371 --> 00:52:11,541
Hold on.

1321
00:52:11,541 --> 00:52:12,701
(Laughing)

1322
00:52:12,971 --> 00:52:14,741
- Hey, this is...
- Wait.

1323
00:52:14,741 --> 00:52:15,911
This is an OB-GYN right here.

1324
00:52:17,881 --> 00:52:22,311
(Seaweed, please hold on.)

1325
00:52:23,321 --> 00:52:27,651
(Mom will get you out in no time.)

1326
00:52:27,891 --> 00:52:30,261
- Darn.
- Okay. Pull it now.

1327
00:52:31,191 --> 00:52:32,321
- One, two.
- Two.

1328
00:52:32,561 --> 00:52:34,861
(Giving the final push)

1329
00:52:35,061 --> 00:52:36,091
Here we go.

1330
00:52:36,331 --> 00:52:37,461
Okay.

1331
00:52:37,461 --> 00:52:39,431
(Grunting)

1332
00:52:39,561 --> 00:52:40,571
(Screaming)

1333
00:52:40,571 --> 00:52:42,231
(The unimaginable pain to give birth to seaweed)

1334
00:52:42,771 --> 00:52:44,701
(After their first seaweed-childbirth,)

1335
00:52:44,871 --> 00:52:46,501
(Grunting, their second seaweed child)

1336
00:52:46,971 --> 00:52:47,971
(Their third seaweed child)

1337
00:52:47,971 --> 00:52:49,011
Gosh. It's a lot.

1338
00:52:49,011 --> 00:52:50,041
(They pushed through, giving birth to seaweed consecutively.)

1339
00:52:50,041 --> 00:52:51,611
Go to the other side.

1340
00:52:51,611 --> 00:52:53,511
(This is not a simple seaweed harvesting.)

1341
00:52:54,051 --> 00:52:57,221
(This is a record of two moms' gruelling seaweed-birth story.)

1342
00:52:57,221 --> 00:52:58,221
Gosh. No.

1343
00:52:58,281 --> 00:52:59,991
I can make a living without working now.

1344
00:53:00,291 --> 00:53:01,521
Okay. Thanks.

1345
00:53:02,791 --> 00:53:03,821
Hold on.

1346
00:53:04,021 --> 00:53:06,121
(Reaching her limit)

1347
00:53:08,761 --> 00:53:10,001
(Mom Sun Young is wiped out.)

1348
00:53:10,001 --> 00:53:11,631
(Laughing)

1349
00:53:11,631 --> 00:53:13,501
- Well...
- My fingers hurt so badly.

1350
00:53:14,801 --> 00:53:15,871
Hold on.

1351
00:53:17,941 --> 00:53:18,941
(While the older sisters feel the pain of giving birth...)

1352
00:53:18,941 --> 00:53:20,111
My fingers.

1353
00:53:22,871 --> 00:53:24,611
Time to put on a disguise.

1354
00:53:24,711 --> 00:53:26,681
- Give me the work clothes.
- Yes. You can change inside.

1355
00:53:27,111 --> 00:53:28,151
What do I...

1356
00:53:28,611 --> 00:53:30,621
- And they'll come up.
- Okay.

1357
00:53:30,621 --> 00:53:31,751
(A man is speaking secretly with the staff.)

1358
00:53:31,981 --> 00:53:32,981
(Breathing in)

1359
00:53:33,421 --> 00:53:36,791
I think I'll get busted.

1360
00:53:37,661 --> 00:53:40,431
(He hurries to disguise himself in work clothes.)

1361
00:53:41,991 --> 00:53:44,901
(Who is this mysterious guy?)

1362
00:53:44,961 --> 00:53:46,201
Yes, put it over there.

1363
00:53:46,201 --> 00:53:47,671
It'll turn yellow.

1364
00:53:47,671 --> 00:53:48,671
(Park Hae Joon?)

1365
00:53:48,671 --> 00:53:50,901
When it's dry, it'll turn yellow.

1366
00:53:50,901 --> 00:53:52,641
Where are they? Are they out in the sea?

1367
00:53:53,971 --> 00:53:55,211
They are having a tough time.

1368
00:53:55,211 --> 00:53:57,541
(A secret guest who has arrived while the siblings are out on boats)

1369
00:53:57,781 --> 00:54:00,611
When I heard the three were on the show,

1370
00:54:00,611 --> 00:54:01,911
I was so happy.

1371
00:54:01,911 --> 00:54:02,951
(He decided to visit right away.)

1372
00:54:03,151 --> 00:54:05,081
I missed them all.

1373
00:54:05,951 --> 00:54:07,421
(Recently, he worked with Jung Ah and Sun Young...)

1374
00:54:07,421 --> 00:54:08,891
(on "Love, Take Two.")

1375
00:54:09,391 --> 00:54:11,091
(He played the father of You Seok...)

1376
00:54:11,091 --> 00:54:12,761
(in "When Life Gives You Tangerines.")

1377
00:54:12,991 --> 00:54:13,991
(Breathing)

1378
00:54:13,991 --> 00:54:16,661
I'm always grateful for You Seok.

1379
00:54:16,961 --> 00:54:18,961
I'm supposed to surprise him, right?

1380
00:54:20,301 --> 00:54:22,001
"I told you not to go on a boat!"

1381
00:54:22,101 --> 00:54:25,401
(That scene is...)

1382
00:54:26,341 --> 00:54:28,611
(It's the scene from "When Life Gives You Tangerines,")

1383
00:54:28,611 --> 00:54:30,881
(where he scolds his son not to get on a boat.)

1384
00:54:31,981 --> 00:54:33,781
(I wanted to get your boat back.)

1385
00:54:36,111 --> 00:54:40,191
(He urged his son not to get on a boat.)

1386
00:54:40,721 --> 00:54:42,121
(But he got on a boat again.)

1387
00:54:42,191 --> 00:54:44,361
"I told you not to go on a boat."

1388
00:54:44,361 --> 00:54:45,721
(He's going to scold You Seok again today.)

1389
00:54:46,661 --> 00:54:47,731
Won't they notice?

1390
00:54:48,391 --> 00:54:50,731
(He gets nervous now that he's about to surprise them.)

1391
00:54:51,331 --> 00:54:53,501
Aren't these too new? Don't they look so new?

1392
00:54:54,531 --> 00:54:56,031
Should I dip myself in the water?

1393
00:54:56,031 --> 00:54:57,401
(Nervous)

1394
00:54:57,641 --> 00:54:59,441
You Seok will come first, right?

1395
00:54:59,671 --> 00:55:01,941
(Shaking his legs out of nervousness)

1396
00:55:02,811 --> 00:55:04,311
He'll find out.

1397
00:55:04,381 --> 00:55:06,381
I shouldn't make eye contact.

1398
00:55:06,881 --> 00:55:08,981
(Pulling his mask closely)

1399
00:55:09,711 --> 00:55:11,681
(Will this prank work?)

1400
00:55:11,681 --> 00:55:12,751
(Sighing)

1401
00:55:14,521 --> 00:55:17,721
(In the meantime, on the older sisters' boat,)

1402
00:55:18,321 --> 00:55:23,431
(they're taking a short break.)

1403
00:55:24,531 --> 00:55:25,631
Jung Ah.

1404
00:55:26,401 --> 00:55:27,701
They're different.

1405
00:55:29,501 --> 00:55:30,741
What's that?

1406
00:55:30,741 --> 00:55:32,001
(The captain's harvesting skill is different.)

1407
00:55:32,541 --> 00:55:33,671
(Amazed)

1408
00:55:33,671 --> 00:55:35,141
(They can't help but be amazed by the amount.)

1409
00:55:35,141 --> 00:55:36,141
(Amazed)

1410
00:55:38,081 --> 00:55:39,181
Look how tall this is.

1411
00:55:40,111 --> 00:55:42,151
- Seriously.
- It's crazy.

1412
00:55:42,151 --> 00:55:43,821
(It's as tall as a human.)

1413
00:55:44,551 --> 00:55:45,981
(Should I get back to it, then?)

1414
00:55:46,821 --> 00:55:47,821
(Captain Yum is motivated by the captain.)

1415
00:55:47,821 --> 00:55:48,851
Gosh.

1416
00:55:50,291 --> 00:55:51,661
(They control the teulitdae with more comfort now.)

1417
00:55:51,661 --> 00:55:53,161
- Seaweed is coming.
- Okay.

1418
00:55:53,891 --> 00:55:55,091
Rotate.

1419
00:55:55,791 --> 00:55:58,501
(They rotate the pole with ease now.)

1420
00:56:00,231 --> 00:56:01,231
I put it close to the boat.

1421
00:56:03,271 --> 00:56:06,541
(The process goes smoothly under Captain Yum's command.)

1422
00:56:07,171 --> 00:56:08,711
(Grunting)

1423
00:56:09,241 --> 00:56:10,341
(Groaning)

1424
00:56:10,981 --> 00:56:13,241
Is it tangled around the pole?

1425
00:56:13,281 --> 00:56:15,451
Gosh. It'll be so heavy.

1426
00:56:15,451 --> 00:56:18,721
(Captain Yum's power starts to show up.)

1427
00:56:20,721 --> 00:56:21,821
It's a lot.

1428
00:56:22,691 --> 00:56:24,861
Gosh. Look at the amount!

1429
00:56:25,391 --> 00:56:27,131
Gosh. This is... Seriously.

1430
00:56:27,691 --> 00:56:28,731
This is really...

1431
00:56:28,731 --> 00:56:30,261
(Plentiful)

1432
00:56:30,631 --> 00:56:31,831
You're good at it now.

1433
00:56:34,231 --> 00:56:36,801
(Should I try it once again?)

1434
00:56:37,601 --> 00:56:40,511
(Going for the 2nd round while keeping the momentum)

1435
00:56:40,971 --> 00:56:42,411
Gosh. These kids.

1436
00:56:42,841 --> 00:56:45,281
(The kids are messing with the wrong person.)

1437
00:56:48,781 --> 00:56:49,781
(Turn me back)

1438
00:56:50,921 --> 00:56:55,521
(To who I was before I met you)

1439
00:56:56,291 --> 00:56:58,291
(To turn it)

1440
00:56:58,291 --> 00:57:00,361
(As memories)

1441
00:57:00,891 --> 00:57:03,931
(She gets hurt by seaweed.)

1442
00:57:04,401 --> 00:57:07,331
(Jung Ah?)

1443
00:57:07,631 --> 00:57:08,631
(Turn me back)

1444
00:57:08,631 --> 00:57:09,831
I can't turn it anymore.

1445
00:57:10,371 --> 00:57:11,441
Come.

1446
00:57:12,771 --> 00:57:14,811
(Sun Young is on the move.)

1447
00:57:15,241 --> 00:57:16,371
(Turn me back)

1448
00:57:16,371 --> 00:57:17,411
I can't spin it.

1449
00:57:17,411 --> 00:57:19,081
(Switching players)

1450
00:57:20,011 --> 00:57:21,111
Look at her.

1451
00:57:21,651 --> 00:57:23,111
Sun Young's so good at it.

1452
00:57:23,451 --> 00:57:25,481
(Grunting)

1453
00:57:26,421 --> 00:57:27,421
(Turn me back)

1454
00:57:27,421 --> 00:57:29,991
(Syncing with Captain Yum's chant,)

1455
00:57:29,991 --> 00:57:31,291
She has incredible arm strength.

1456
00:57:31,291 --> 00:57:32,921
(Sun Young is now quick and efficient.)

1457
00:57:34,291 --> 00:57:37,431
(Spinning it like crazy)

1458
00:57:37,901 --> 00:57:38,931
You're good.

1459
00:57:39,961 --> 00:57:41,571
You can live on Geoje Island now.

1460
00:57:41,831 --> 00:57:43,841
(They finally won the right to move to Geoje Island.)

1461
00:57:44,171 --> 00:57:45,201
Let's pull it out now.

1462
00:57:46,371 --> 00:57:47,671
(Screaming)

1463
00:57:48,111 --> 00:57:49,311
(Amazed)

1464
00:57:50,511 --> 00:57:54,051
(They harvested as much seaweed as the captain did.)

1465
00:57:54,311 --> 00:57:55,911
(Straining)

1466
00:57:56,381 --> 00:58:01,091
(The older sisters have mastered the seaweed harvest skills.)

1467
00:58:01,721 --> 00:58:02,821
- Okay.
- Okay.

1468
00:58:02,821 --> 00:58:04,391
- Let's beat them.
- I know how to do it now.

1469
00:58:05,161 --> 00:58:06,161
(Groaning)

1470
00:58:06,161 --> 00:58:08,691
(The younger siblings put more effort in after that.)

1471
00:58:08,931 --> 00:58:10,931
- Do you need help?
- I think I'm fine.

1472
00:58:11,831 --> 00:58:13,331
- Take it out if it's too hard.
- No.

1473
00:58:14,601 --> 00:58:15,601
It's fun.

1474
00:58:17,701 --> 00:58:19,471
I won't be responsible if you have body aches.

1475
00:58:19,471 --> 00:58:20,941
(Somewhere between positivity and madness)

1476
00:58:21,741 --> 00:58:23,841
- It's so heavy.
- Let's see.

1477
00:58:24,011 --> 00:58:25,311
(Screaming)

1478
00:58:25,311 --> 00:58:26,381
It's a lot.

1479
00:58:27,251 --> 00:58:28,281
It's plentiful.

1480
00:58:28,581 --> 00:58:30,681
(She caught a big catch again.)

1481
00:58:30,681 --> 00:58:31,781
Good job.

1482
00:58:32,021 --> 00:58:33,121
(Laughing)

1483
00:58:33,421 --> 00:58:34,621
(Smiling)

1484
00:58:34,621 --> 00:58:35,821
(Scared)

1485
00:58:37,591 --> 00:58:39,091
You're so good at shaking off too.

1486
00:58:39,921 --> 00:58:41,491
- I'm amazing, aren't I?
- Let's get a boat.

1487
00:58:41,491 --> 00:58:42,531
Shall we?

1488
00:58:42,531 --> 00:58:43,561
(Bragging)

1489
00:58:43,761 --> 00:58:46,131
- I'll become a seaweed master.
- You're shaking it off well.

1490
00:58:46,131 --> 00:58:47,301
(Seaweed Master Yoon Seo gives the seaweed a good shake.)

1491
00:58:47,301 --> 00:58:48,431
Gosh. It's so fresh.

1492
00:58:51,601 --> 00:58:52,601
(Grunting)

1493
00:58:54,571 --> 00:58:55,571
(Grunting)

1494
00:58:55,571 --> 00:58:56,771
(You Seok's gotten the hang of it, except for the grunting.)

1495
00:58:56,771 --> 00:58:58,241
You're a tough guy.

1496
00:59:00,211 --> 00:59:01,881
We're getting the hang of it, You Seok.

1497
00:59:01,881 --> 00:59:03,111
Yes. You're good at it now.

1498
00:59:04,251 --> 00:59:06,181
- Gosh. Look at you, You Seok.
- Gosh, You Seok.

1499
00:59:07,521 --> 00:59:09,251
- He's finally earning his keep.
- You Seok.

1500
00:59:10,021 --> 00:59:11,821
At this rate, you'd be able to work on your own soon.

1501
00:59:11,821 --> 00:59:13,591
(The younger siblings are harvesting with ease too.)

1502
00:59:13,591 --> 00:59:14,931
- You Seok.
- I got it now.

1503
00:59:15,261 --> 00:59:16,361
Do you get it now?

1504
00:59:16,591 --> 00:59:18,961
I'm going to quit my job in Seoul and come here...

1505
00:59:18,961 --> 00:59:20,671
- Yes, you can do that.
- to harvest seaweed with you.

1506
00:59:21,871 --> 00:59:23,771
Don't go. You're all mine.

1507
00:59:23,771 --> 00:59:24,771
They're all ours.

1508
00:59:25,401 --> 00:59:26,401
(Amazed)

1509
00:59:26,901 --> 00:59:27,971
Good job.

1510
00:59:27,971 --> 00:59:29,111
- Gosh.
- I'm a master now.

1511
00:59:29,971 --> 00:59:32,411
