1765
01:09:45,911 --> 01:09:50,751
(It's not a sin to fall in love with seaweed soup.)

1766
01:09:51,291 --> 01:09:53,921
Tomorrow, we're having a cooking competition.

1767
01:09:54,421 --> 01:09:55,421
A cooking competition.

1768
01:09:56,661 --> 01:09:58,431
(One month ago, during the introductory meeting)

1769
01:09:59,491 --> 01:10:01,461
(The younger members wanted to cook for Jung Ah.)

1770
01:10:01,761 --> 01:10:02,931
(What do you like, Jung Ah?)

1771
01:10:03,161 --> 01:10:04,201
(I like curry!)

1772
01:10:04,931 --> 01:10:07,001
(Jung Ah, you have no idea how great of curry I make.)

1773
01:10:07,001 --> 01:10:08,641
(I'm an expert when it comes to curry.)

1774
01:10:09,141 --> 01:10:12,111
(Everyone is claiming themselves a curry master.)

1775
01:10:12,341 --> 01:10:14,211
(I'll start by caramelizing onions...)

1776
01:10:14,211 --> 01:10:15,441
(and cook it Japanese-style.)

1777
01:10:15,981 --> 01:10:18,551
(Caramelizing onions?)

1778
01:10:18,811 --> 01:10:19,811
(I don't do stuff like that.)

1779
01:10:20,051 --> 01:10:22,181
(That's not how you cook curry.)

1780
01:10:22,781 --> 01:10:24,751
(Sun Young, I have a feeling yours will taste bad.)

1781
01:10:25,451 --> 01:10:26,521
- Why?
- It'll taste plain.

1782
01:10:26,521 --> 01:10:27,591
(Insulted)

1783
01:10:27,791 --> 01:10:28,861
(That's not true.)

1784
01:10:29,191 --> 01:10:30,691
(Shall we make it a curry competition?)

1785
01:10:32,561 --> 01:10:34,501
(Shall we do a curry competition?)

1786
01:10:34,661 --> 01:10:35,731
I could never lose.

1787
01:10:35,731 --> 01:10:37,331
(It provoked the gamer's competitiveness.)

1788
01:10:37,971 --> 01:10:40,971
(I'll learn from a chef.)

1789
01:10:41,971 --> 01:10:44,741
(The curry competition has suddenly been decided.)

1790
01:10:45,541 --> 01:10:47,141
- Curry?
- That's the menu.

1791
01:10:47,541 --> 01:10:48,811
And I'm sitting it out.

1792
01:10:49,741 --> 01:10:50,981
They'll be joining. You should participate.

1793
01:10:51,651 --> 01:10:53,551
I'll definitely win.

1794
01:10:53,551 --> 01:10:57,421
(If I participate, I'll definitely win!)

1795
01:10:58,091 --> 01:11:00,391
- Do you cook often at home?
- Curry is easy.

1796
01:11:01,621 --> 01:11:04,261
(Actually, Hae Joon is...)

1797
01:11:04,661 --> 01:11:07,461
I'm not a bad cook.

1798
01:11:07,461 --> 01:11:09,231
- Are you good with knives?
- I'm not bad.

1799
01:11:11,271 --> 01:11:13,501
(He cuts radish with ease.)

1800
01:11:14,001 --> 01:11:19,071
(He mastered from bossam to rice cake soup.)

1801
01:11:19,711 --> 01:11:22,181
(The genius chef lost to the culinary world)

1802
01:11:23,041 --> 01:11:24,381
We can buy curry powder, right?

1803
01:11:24,651 --> 01:11:26,711
Of course. You need curry powder.

1804
01:11:27,281 --> 01:11:29,621
Which brand of curry will you use?

1805
01:11:29,621 --> 01:11:30,721
Or will it be Japanese-style?

1806
01:11:30,721 --> 01:11:31,751
(Listing out the types of curry)

1807
01:11:31,751 --> 01:11:33,221
Or hayashi rice?

1808
01:11:34,461 --> 01:11:35,661
(Look at him.)

1809
01:11:35,891 --> 01:11:37,791
- He's cooked it a lot.
- Of course.

1810
01:11:38,891 --> 01:11:41,701
Do you like beef, pork, or chicken?

1811
01:11:42,661 --> 01:11:44,101
You shouldn't tell him.

1812
01:11:46,171 --> 01:11:47,431
He sounds like a professional.

1813
01:11:48,741 --> 01:11:49,901
I'll end up in last place at this rate.

1814
01:11:49,901 --> 01:11:51,511
(Whining)

1815
01:11:52,071 --> 01:11:55,881
(Who will win the curry competition?)

1816
01:11:56,541 --> 01:11:57,581
How much...

1817
01:11:58,251 --> 01:11:59,281
are you giving us today?

1818
01:11:59,651 --> 01:12:00,711
Right.

1819
01:12:02,121 --> 01:12:03,151
How much are you giving us today?

1820
01:12:03,151 --> 01:12:05,521
(Very serious)

1821
01:12:05,891 --> 01:12:08,421
You should tell us how much we'll get for the work.

1822
01:12:08,961 --> 01:12:11,861
Even here, all Eun Myeong talks about is money.

1823
01:12:13,131 --> 01:12:14,661
(Suddenly back to "When Life Gives You Tangerines")

1824
01:12:14,661 --> 01:12:15,731
Eun Myeong.

1825
01:12:17,261 --> 01:12:18,631
- Father.
- Yes.

1826
01:12:18,901 --> 01:12:20,331
I'm trying to get your boat back.

1827
01:12:22,101 --> 01:12:26,441
(The dad is worried about his son.)

1828
01:12:27,041 --> 01:12:30,241
(The son wanted to get his boat back by harvesting seaweed.)

1829
01:12:30,741 --> 01:12:35,881
(The story of the good son Eun Myeong)

1830
01:12:36,381 --> 01:12:39,751
(I want the sequel.)

1831
01:12:40,621 --> 01:12:42,861
Do you like to jog? Will you join me tomorrow morning?

1832
01:12:44,391 --> 01:12:46,331
He's thinking about running tomorrow,

1833
01:12:47,231 --> 01:12:48,261
which means the work wasn't tough enough.

1834
01:12:49,561 --> 01:12:52,631
The work wasn't tough enough. We should run him into the ground...

1835
01:12:52,801 --> 01:12:53,871
so he can't run tomorrow.

1836
01:12:53,871 --> 01:12:55,371
(Terrified)

1837
01:12:56,041 --> 01:12:58,411
I didn't even think about it because I was set on working hard.

1838
01:12:59,271 --> 01:13:01,541
(Laughing)

1839
01:13:02,111 --> 01:13:05,081
(Gwan Sik attacks Eun Myeong fiercely.)

1840
01:13:05,751 --> 01:13:08,121
(It suddenly turned into a comedy.)

1841
01:13:08,621 --> 01:13:10,921
Eun Myeong, can I have more seaweed?

1842
01:13:12,091 --> 01:13:13,121
Can I have more seaweed too?

1843
01:13:13,121 --> 01:13:14,191
(The refill request continues.)

1844
01:13:14,491 --> 01:13:17,121
(It recharged them good after the hard work.)

1845
01:13:17,661 --> 01:13:20,631
(It was a fun mealtime.)

1846
01:13:21,031 --> 01:13:22,031
(They've finished two bowls each.)

1847
01:13:22,031 --> 01:13:23,961
This would sell so well.

1848
01:13:24,931 --> 01:13:27,201
I'm so full. I ate so much seaweed.

1849
01:13:28,141 --> 01:13:30,341
(Sun Young suddenly stands up.)

1850
01:13:30,871 --> 01:13:33,171
(She warms up slowly.)

1851
01:13:33,641 --> 01:13:36,011
Jung Ah taught me the workout which prevents backaches.

1852
01:13:37,141 --> 01:13:38,181
It prevents backaches.

1853
01:13:40,181 --> 01:13:41,521
Instructor, am I doing it right?

1854
01:13:42,581 --> 01:13:45,891
It is. Just do as you like.

1855
01:13:45,891 --> 01:13:47,221
(Just do however you feel like doing.)

1856
01:13:47,721 --> 01:13:50,761
- Did you learn it from someone?
- No, I made it myself.

1857
01:13:53,391 --> 01:13:55,661
It really helps you strengthen your back.

1858
01:13:55,661 --> 01:13:56,661
(Yoon Seo joins her.)

1859
01:13:57,131 --> 01:14:00,831
(Dancing)

1860
01:14:00,831 --> 01:14:02,701
- My back hurts too.
- Do this if your back hurts.

1861
01:14:03,741 --> 01:14:08,241
(Gosh, you guys...)

1862
01:14:09,381 --> 01:14:10,511
You need to pop your hips.

1863
01:14:10,511 --> 01:14:11,681
(Hae Joon joins the exercise.)

1864
01:14:12,051 --> 01:14:14,051
- Not front and back?
- No. It feels nice.

1865
01:14:14,051 --> 01:14:16,451
(I'm excited.)

1866
01:14:16,851 --> 01:14:17,891
Instructor.

1867
01:14:17,891 --> 01:14:20,151
(Unable to resist, Jung Ah joins them too.)

1868
01:14:20,691 --> 01:14:23,661
- My hips are...
- I'm so excited.

1869
01:14:23,661 --> 01:14:25,761
(A dancing machine)

1870
01:14:26,261 --> 01:14:30,731
(Are you sure? My hips don't know how to stop.)

1871
01:14:31,301 --> 01:14:33,971
- Your back doesn't hurt, right?
- It stretches nicely.

1872
01:14:34,801 --> 01:14:36,001
(Wiggling)

1873
01:14:36,001 --> 01:14:37,041
It feels nice.

1874
01:14:37,571 --> 01:14:38,911
The ladies must be wondering what we're doing.

1875
01:14:38,911 --> 01:14:40,941
(Laughing)

1876
01:14:42,411 --> 01:14:44,581
- They're following our dance.
- Where?

1877
01:14:45,211 --> 01:14:47,481
They're doing it too.

1878
01:14:47,481 --> 01:14:48,821
The dance spread so quickly.

1879
01:14:48,821 --> 01:14:50,351
(I heard it was fun.)

1880
01:14:50,351 --> 01:14:52,851
Yes, do it when your back hurts.

1881
01:14:52,851 --> 01:14:54,861
(Dance)

1882
01:14:57,421 --> 01:14:59,461
(Join us.)

1883
01:14:59,461 --> 01:15:00,461
My gosh.

1884
01:15:00,891 --> 01:15:02,431
- Thank you for the food.
- Thank you for the food.

1885
01:15:03,131 --> 01:15:04,531
- It was the best.
- This is so funny.

1886
01:15:04,831 --> 01:15:05,931
(It's time to work again.)

1887
01:15:05,931 --> 01:15:07,001
Let's hang the seaweed up.

1888
01:15:07,001 --> 01:15:08,071
(Let's hang the seaweed up.)

1889
01:15:08,471 --> 01:15:09,571
Hello.

1890
01:15:09,571 --> 01:15:11,111
- Hello.
- Hello.

1891
01:15:12,341 --> 01:15:13,541
Shall we hang up...

1892
01:15:13,841 --> 01:15:14,841
- Yes.
- Yes.

1893
01:15:14,841 --> 01:15:15,881
the seaweed you harvested from the sea?

1894
01:15:15,881 --> 01:15:17,041
- Okay.
- Okay.

1895
01:15:17,911 --> 01:15:20,151
(Seaweed labour Step 2: Drying the seaweed)

1896
01:15:20,611 --> 01:15:21,751
(Freshly caught moist wild rock seaweed)

1897
01:15:21,751 --> 01:15:23,681
We go out on a boat and harvest them.

1898
01:15:25,351 --> 01:15:29,721
(Cut off the holdfast of seaweed.)

1899
01:15:30,661 --> 01:15:32,031
And we dry them all.

1900
01:15:32,031 --> 01:15:36,761
(Hang them up on the drier one by one.)

1901
01:15:40,901 --> 01:15:46,671
(Under the warm sun of Gyeonnaeryang,)

1902
01:15:46,671 --> 01:15:50,141
We need to dry them for three days to be able to sell them.

1903
01:15:50,141 --> 01:15:51,651
(dry them out for 3 days.)

1904
01:15:53,351 --> 01:15:56,721
(Tasty and healthy wild rock seaweed is completed.)

1905
01:15:56,721 --> 01:15:58,691
It's dried naturally under the sun,

1906
01:15:58,691 --> 01:16:00,051
so it's yellowish.

1907
01:16:00,051 --> 01:16:04,491
(It's yellowish because it's dried under the sun.)

1908
01:16:05,761 --> 01:16:08,661
(Shall we start the work?)

1909
01:16:09,301 --> 01:16:13,431
(The first step to dry the seaweed: Setting up a drying rack)

1910
01:16:13,901 --> 01:16:15,241
Put it here.

1911
01:16:15,241 --> 01:16:16,541
- Put it here.
- Okay.

1912
01:16:16,541 --> 01:16:17,541
(Carrying it)

1913
01:16:17,541 --> 01:16:19,141
Stand facing each other.

1914
01:16:19,141 --> 01:16:20,171
- Yes.
- Yes.

1915
01:16:21,181 --> 01:16:23,541
- Do I spread them out?
- Yes, spread them out.

1916
01:16:23,541 --> 01:16:24,811
(Spread out the seaweed to dry.)

1917
01:16:25,211 --> 01:16:26,281
Spread them out evenly.

1918
01:16:26,281 --> 01:16:27,351
(Seaweed-drying Tip 1)

1919
01:16:27,351 --> 01:16:28,451
(Spread them out evenly so they will dry well.)

1920
01:16:28,851 --> 01:16:29,881
Evenly.

1921
01:16:29,881 --> 01:16:31,821
(Inputs "evenly")

1922
01:16:32,321 --> 01:16:34,451
(Flatten)

1923
01:16:34,761 --> 01:16:37,591
(Outputs "evenly")

1924
01:16:37,691 --> 01:16:39,361
Do I fill up the corner as well?

1925
01:16:39,361 --> 01:16:40,531
Yes.

1926
01:16:40,531 --> 01:16:43,101
They'll shrink as they dry up.

1927
01:16:43,101 --> 01:16:44,161
(Seaweed shrinks as it dries up.)

1928
01:16:44,301 --> 01:16:45,701
They shrink a lot when they dry up.

1929
01:16:45,701 --> 01:16:46,871
(You must fill up the whole rack without any empty spot.)

1930
01:16:47,731 --> 01:16:49,101
They shrink like that.

1931
01:16:49,101 --> 01:16:50,341
(That's how you make pretty seaweed.)

1932
01:16:50,541 --> 01:16:52,811
Is this thick enough?

1933
01:16:52,811 --> 01:16:54,011
No, make it thicker.

1934
01:16:54,011 --> 01:16:55,981
- Thicker?
- Or there will be holes.

1935
01:16:55,981 --> 01:16:57,241
- We can't have holes?
- No holes at all.

1936
01:16:57,241 --> 01:16:58,911
- Cover up all the empty spots.
- I see.

1937
01:16:58,911 --> 01:16:59,911
(Seaweed-drying Tip 2: Pile them up nice and thick.)

1938
01:17:00,081 --> 01:17:01,721
But not too thick.

1939
01:17:01,721 --> 01:17:02,951
It won't dry up.

1940
01:17:02,951 --> 01:17:04,181
(But it can't be too thick.)

1941
01:17:04,521 --> 01:17:08,291
(You must maintain the right thickness.)

1942
01:17:08,821 --> 01:17:10,891
The big ones don't dry up easily.

1943
01:17:11,961 --> 01:17:14,161
Cut up the big ones.

1944
01:17:14,161 --> 01:17:15,331
- Okay.
- Okay.

1945
01:17:16,031 --> 01:17:18,131
- They don't dry up easily.
- Yes.

1946
01:17:18,131 --> 01:17:19,631
(Laughing)

1947
01:17:19,631 --> 01:17:21,171
- She's a copycat.
- Yes.

1948
01:17:22,301 --> 01:17:23,801
How long have you worked here?

1949
01:17:23,901 --> 01:17:26,111
- Around a decade for me.
- A decade?

1950
01:17:26,841 --> 01:17:27,841
"For me."

1951
01:17:27,841 --> 01:17:29,211
"For me."

1952
01:17:29,211 --> 01:17:30,781
(Her lies are on a whole new level.)

1953
01:17:31,011 --> 01:17:32,151
Ma'am, is this good enough?

1954
01:17:32,151 --> 01:17:34,951
No, you need more, mister.

1955
01:17:34,951 --> 01:17:36,451
Bring more.

1956
01:17:36,451 --> 01:17:37,451
The small one.

1957
01:17:37,721 --> 01:17:39,051
Here you go.

1958
01:17:39,051 --> 01:17:40,221
- That's enough.
- Yes.

1959
01:17:40,791 --> 01:17:44,691
(Very thorough)

1960
01:17:45,431 --> 01:17:47,291
I hope they dry well.

1961
01:17:47,291 --> 01:17:48,861
(Pressing them firmly)

1962
01:17:49,061 --> 01:17:52,101
Ma'am, is this all right?

1963
01:17:52,101 --> 01:17:53,371
I don't think you've worked for a decade.

1964
01:17:53,371 --> 01:17:54,671
You don't think so?

1965
01:17:56,701 --> 01:17:59,611
(Attacking her with facts)

1966
01:17:59,871 --> 01:18:00,871
Ma'am.

1967
01:18:00,871 --> 01:18:02,411
(Upset)

1968
01:18:02,741 --> 01:18:06,051
(Come back after 10 years.)

1969
01:18:07,211 --> 01:18:08,721
- Here.
- Thank you.

1970
01:18:08,721 --> 01:18:09,721
(They spread them out one by one.)

1971
01:18:10,181 --> 01:18:11,591
(The rack is very full.)

1972
01:18:11,591 --> 01:18:12,821
It's so full.

1973
01:18:13,551 --> 01:18:15,261
- Lift it up...
- Yes.

1974
01:18:15,261 --> 01:18:16,361
and move it to there.

1975
01:18:16,361 --> 01:18:17,621
- Over there?
- Yes.

1976
01:18:17,621 --> 01:18:18,631
(It's time to move the drying rack to a sunny spot.)

1977
01:18:18,631 --> 01:18:19,661
Hold there.

1978
01:18:19,931 --> 01:18:21,231
Careful.

1979
01:18:21,231 --> 01:18:22,231
(They start moving.)

1980
01:18:25,171 --> 01:18:26,601
There are legs underneath.

1981
01:18:28,641 --> 01:18:30,441
- The legs.
- Unfold them.

1982
01:18:30,441 --> 01:18:33,711
(Unfold the legs and put it down nicely.)

1983
01:18:34,341 --> 01:18:35,541
That's good. Enough space for people to walk around.

1984
01:18:35,541 --> 01:18:37,611
Okay, enough space for people to walk around.

1985
01:18:38,551 --> 01:18:41,551
(The first rack is completed.)

1986
01:18:41,851 --> 01:18:44,521
They must dry up well since it's very sunny nowadays.

1987
01:18:45,391 --> 01:18:46,951
Here comes more seaweed.

1988
01:18:46,951 --> 01:18:49,461
(Without catching a breath, they start on the next rack.)

1989
01:18:49,761 --> 01:18:52,961
I'll make it as pretty as possible.

1990
01:18:53,861 --> 01:18:57,401
(Meanwhile, Hae Joon is very enthusiastic.)

1991
01:18:57,601 --> 01:19:00,071
When you get married, you must have this seaweed.

1992
01:19:00,071 --> 01:19:03,941
(When you get married, you must have this seaweed.)

1993
01:19:04,271 --> 01:19:05,811
Yes, I will.

1994
01:19:06,211 --> 01:19:07,611
He's yet to get married.

1995
01:19:07,611 --> 01:19:09,341
(She thinks Hae Joon is a bachelor, but he's been married for 16 years.)

1996
01:19:09,341 --> 01:19:11,041
Goodness.

1997
01:19:11,041 --> 01:19:13,181
I would've gotten married already if I was good at making seaweed.

1998
01:19:13,181 --> 01:19:15,351
She saw you...

1999
01:19:15,351 --> 01:19:17,321
and thought you were a bachelor.

2000
01:19:17,321 --> 01:19:18,921
Yes. I'd get married right away.

2001
01:19:18,921 --> 01:19:19,951
(The seaweed bachelor feels happy.)

2002
01:19:19,951 --> 01:19:22,191
The bachelor will fill up this side of the rack.

2003
01:19:22,591 --> 01:19:24,661
(He's so funny.)

2004
01:19:24,961 --> 01:19:27,731
(But...)

2005
01:19:28,101 --> 01:19:30,401
(Piled up)

2006
01:19:31,601 --> 01:19:33,701
(There's just no end to the seaweed.)

2007
01:19:33,701 --> 01:19:34,871
There's more?

2008
01:19:35,241 --> 01:19:37,271
This takes a lot of effort.

2009
01:19:37,271 --> 01:19:38,571
It does.

2010
01:19:40,271 --> 01:19:42,481
It'll be very gruelling if you do this for a long time.

2011
01:19:42,481 --> 01:19:44,041
(You must spread out heavy seaweed under the burning sun.)

2012
01:19:44,681 --> 01:19:46,451
Goodness.

2013
01:19:46,451 --> 01:19:48,651
(It's hard for the passionate bachelor too.)

2014
01:19:48,981 --> 01:19:50,381
I thought nothing of it when I bought them.

2015
01:19:50,381 --> 01:19:51,991
(This is a seaweed nightmare.)

2016
01:19:51,991 --> 01:19:53,591
I thought this would be easy.

2017
01:19:53,591 --> 01:19:54,721
But it isn't.

2018
01:19:55,561 --> 01:19:58,361
(While everyone is struggling in the seaweed nightmare)

2019
01:19:59,331 --> 01:20:00,831
- Does it look like hair?
- It swishes.

2020
01:20:02,261 --> 01:20:04,731
Ma'am, I'd already put it here.

2021
01:20:05,531 --> 01:20:06,901
You can't take what I put here.

2022
01:20:07,131 --> 01:20:08,301
I stole it.

2023
01:20:08,301 --> 01:20:09,771
(Playful Yoon Seo steals You Seok's seaweed.)

2024
01:20:10,271 --> 01:20:12,241
Now I understand why people compare hair to raw seaweed.

2025
01:20:13,011 --> 01:20:14,311
It swishes a lot.

2026
01:20:15,541 --> 01:20:17,781
Swish.

2027
01:20:17,781 --> 01:20:19,051
(Like a baby doing a tactile play)

2028
01:20:19,251 --> 01:20:20,751
Seaweed.

2029
01:20:20,751 --> 01:20:22,021
(Yoon Seo is fascinated by the seaweed's texture.)

2030
01:20:22,021 --> 01:20:23,051
Goodness.

2031
01:20:24,251 --> 01:20:25,991
- Aren't you tired, Yoon Seo?
- No.

2032
01:20:27,351 --> 01:20:28,621
It's like making kimchi.

2033
01:20:29,621 --> 01:20:32,091
(Very goofy)

2034
01:20:32,361 --> 01:20:33,931
Where's the gap?

2035
01:20:34,831 --> 01:20:36,131
Don't show any gap.

2036
01:20:36,731 --> 01:20:37,761
Fill up the gaps.

2037
01:20:37,761 --> 01:20:38,801
(A cute threat to the seaweed)

2038
01:20:38,801 --> 01:20:41,001
(She's adorable.)

2039
01:20:41,271 --> 01:20:44,671
(The lovely youngest never stops smiling.)

2040
01:20:44,911 --> 01:20:45,941
- Let's go.
- Is it done?

2041
01:20:45,941 --> 01:20:47,141
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

2042
01:20:47,141 --> 01:20:48,341
One, two, three.

2043
01:20:48,581 --> 01:20:49,711
Watch your step.

2044
01:20:49,911 --> 01:20:51,211
My goodness.

2045
01:20:51,211 --> 01:20:52,451
(As they spread them out excitedly, they complete another rack.)

2046
01:20:52,511 --> 01:20:53,681
I should use more.

2047
01:20:53,681 --> 01:20:55,081
- Do you need more seaweed?
- Yes.

2048
01:20:55,481 --> 01:20:56,551
There are a lot of gaps.

2049
01:20:56,551 --> 01:20:58,221
(They continue to hang up the seaweed thoroughly.)

2050
01:20:58,421 --> 01:21:00,721
All of you are so good.

2051
01:21:00,721 --> 01:21:01,821
Really?

2052
01:21:01,821 --> 01:21:02,891
Thank you.

2053
01:21:02,891 --> 01:21:04,221
(They all look like experts now.)

2054
01:21:04,561 --> 01:21:08,431
(They fill up the drying racks together.)

2055
01:21:08,631 --> 01:21:10,561
- They're getting closer to us.
- Yes.

2056
01:21:10,561 --> 01:21:11,631
Goodness.

2057
01:21:12,001 --> 01:21:13,131
We filled up everything.

2058
01:21:13,131 --> 01:21:14,631
(Heave-ho)

2059
01:21:15,171 --> 01:21:17,541
- It feels a bit like farming.
- Yes.

2060
01:21:17,871 --> 01:21:18,971
Farming? Yes.

2061
01:21:18,971 --> 01:21:20,541
Like ploughing the field.

2062
01:21:21,941 --> 01:21:26,151
(Is the seaweed drying well?)

2063
01:21:26,902 --> 01:21:28,312
I feel satisfied looking at them.

2064
01:21:28,312 --> 01:21:30,912
(Just looking at them makes her feel satisfied.)

2065
01:21:31,272 --> 01:21:32,842
Is this the last one?

2066
01:21:32,842 --> 01:21:34,382
- It's already the last one.
- Really?

2067
01:21:34,382 --> 01:21:35,482
(It's their last rack already.)

2068
01:21:35,782 --> 01:21:37,382
Since we work on it together...

2069
01:21:37,382 --> 01:21:39,422
- It's over quickly.
- It's over quickly.

2070
01:21:40,252 --> 01:21:43,122
You bond over work.

2071
01:21:43,192 --> 01:21:45,692
- And over a meal.
- Yes.

2072
01:21:46,362 --> 01:21:48,292
- You bond over work.
- Over work.

2073
01:21:48,892 --> 01:21:50,792
The weather is nice. This village is so lively.

2074
01:21:50,792 --> 01:21:51,862
- It's so pretty.
- Yes.

2075
01:21:51,862 --> 01:21:53,602
(The siblings' bond thickens today.)

2076
01:21:54,102 --> 01:21:57,232
(They scrape up the remaining seaweed...)

2077
01:21:57,372 --> 01:22:02,112
(and press it down together.)

2078
01:22:02,472 --> 01:22:05,082
- Let's go now.
- Let's go.

2079
01:22:05,082 --> 01:22:06,242
(The final rack is completed.)

2080
01:22:06,742 --> 01:22:07,842
The final one.

2081
01:22:08,312 --> 01:22:09,512
We're done.

2082
01:22:10,852 --> 01:22:12,722
- Right here.
- We're done.

2083
01:22:12,752 --> 01:22:14,182
- Yoon Seo, watch your back.
- Okay.

2084
01:22:14,182 --> 01:22:15,192
(The siblings filled up 9 racks.)

2085
01:22:16,292 --> 01:22:18,022
(The end of the seaweed labour)

2086
01:22:18,022 --> 01:22:21,392
Everyone, do the back dance.

2087
01:22:21,422 --> 01:22:24,632
Good job with the seaweed labour.

2088
01:22:25,032 --> 01:22:26,662
I'll pay you the wage.

2089
01:22:26,662 --> 01:22:28,002
- Okay.
- Thank you.

2090
01:22:28,162 --> 01:22:29,272
- How much is it?
- How much?

2091
01:22:29,272 --> 01:22:30,302
(Payment time)

2092
01:22:30,302 --> 01:22:31,572
They said wild rock seaweed was expensive.

2093
01:22:31,572 --> 01:22:33,542
- Wild rock seaweed is expensive.
- And five of us worked.

2094
01:22:34,142 --> 01:22:35,942
And spinning that thing was so hard.

2095
01:22:35,942 --> 01:22:37,542
My gosh, how much is that?

2096
01:22:38,112 --> 01:22:39,482
- How much is it?
- That's a lot.

2097
01:22:39,482 --> 01:22:41,042
- Three.
- Three hundred?

2098
01:22:41,142 --> 01:22:42,212
Two hundred.

2099
01:22:42,212 --> 01:22:43,382
(200 dollars in total)

2100
01:22:43,382 --> 01:22:44,582
Two hundred?

2101
01:22:44,582 --> 01:22:46,622
We're rich.

2102
01:22:47,022 --> 01:22:48,892
We earned more than yesterday, right?

2103
01:22:49,952 --> 01:22:51,122
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

2104
01:22:51,122 --> 01:22:52,392
- Two hundred dollars.
- Thank you.

2105
01:22:52,392 --> 01:22:53,562
(Super elated)

2106
01:22:54,122 --> 01:22:55,992
Thank you for your hard work.

2107
01:22:56,092 --> 01:22:57,332
- Goodness.
- Thank you.

2108
01:22:58,132 --> 01:22:59,802
- Thank you.
- I hope you enjoy it.

2109
01:22:59,802 --> 01:23:01,772
- Such precious seaweed.
- Thank you so much.

2110
01:23:01,772 --> 01:23:02,832
(Her gift for the siblings who worked hard)

2111
01:23:03,002 --> 01:23:04,402
- This is...
- What is it?

2112
01:23:04,902 --> 01:23:09,472
(Gyeonnaeryang wild rock seaweed fresh off the sea)

2113
01:23:09,772 --> 01:23:11,442
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

2114
01:23:11,442 --> 01:23:13,442
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

2115
01:23:14,342 --> 01:23:17,012
(3 days later)

2116
01:23:17,912 --> 01:23:21,652
(The seaweed harvested by the siblings...)

2117
01:23:22,092 --> 01:23:25,422
(were dried well...)

2118
01:23:25,992 --> 01:23:32,662
(under the warm sunlight of Gyeonnaeryang.)

2119
01:23:34,902 --> 01:23:39,042
(They became tasty wild rock seaweed and were shipped nationwide.)

2120
01:23:40,202 --> 01:23:41,912
It was very laborious.

2121
01:23:42,142 --> 01:23:43,242
We worked hard today.

2122
01:23:43,812 --> 01:23:46,312
Before we go back,

2123
01:23:48,852 --> 01:23:50,512
remember the deal...

2124
01:23:50,512 --> 01:23:52,122
you've made with us?

2125
01:23:53,452 --> 01:23:54,622
The weather is nice.

2126
01:23:54,722 --> 01:23:57,252
It'll be perfect to ride the cable car and the luge.

2127
01:23:57,422 --> 01:23:58,892
Can I make a 1-on-1 deal with the staff?

2128
01:23:59,322 --> 01:24:01,592
He said he could never lose in omok.

2129
01:24:01,592 --> 01:24:03,532
If you beat him in omok.

2130
01:24:03,532 --> 01:24:05,232
(He suggested an omok match with the luge on the line.)

2131
01:24:05,732 --> 01:24:07,702
A game of omok now?

2132
01:24:07,762 --> 01:24:08,932
- Here?
- Here?

2133
01:24:08,932 --> 01:24:11,432
(But...)

2134
01:24:11,432 --> 01:24:13,702
- We're going to ride the luge?
- Right now?

2135
01:24:14,072 --> 01:24:15,112
We're going to ride the luge?

2136
01:24:15,112 --> 01:24:17,112
(It's bad news for Sun Young, who has used up her energy.)

2137
01:24:17,742 --> 01:24:18,942
Sun Young...

2138
01:24:18,942 --> 01:24:20,582
(She's exhausted.)

2139
01:24:21,012 --> 01:24:23,312
(Walking slowly)

2140
01:24:23,312 --> 01:24:25,752
- It's 35 dollars.
- Lose.

2141
01:24:26,752 --> 01:24:29,722
She told you to lose.

2142
01:24:30,422 --> 01:24:31,762
She did this.

2143
01:24:31,922 --> 01:24:33,322
They're so scary.

2144
01:24:34,092 --> 01:24:35,532
- Just You Seok.
- A quick match.

2145
01:24:35,532 --> 01:24:37,162
Go and play.

2146
01:24:37,162 --> 01:24:38,362
We'll set off first.

2147
01:24:38,362 --> 01:24:39,362
I'll get going.

2148
01:24:39,362 --> 01:24:41,632
- We elected the players too.
- Yes.

2149
01:24:41,632 --> 01:24:43,502
- We have three candidates.
- Okay.

2150
01:24:43,502 --> 01:24:45,872
- Out of the three candidates, - Do we choose?

2151
01:24:45,872 --> 01:24:47,972
choose one after hearing their keywords.

2152
01:24:47,972 --> 01:24:49,112
- Choose one.
- You'll play against them.

2153
01:24:49,712 --> 01:24:50,712
Sounds good.

2154
01:24:51,312 --> 01:24:52,512
Sounds good.

2155
01:24:52,642 --> 01:24:55,312
We need to choose someone who is bad at it.

2156
01:24:55,312 --> 01:24:57,782
Number one, a global leader.

2157
01:24:57,782 --> 01:24:59,522
(Opponent candidate 1: A global leader)

2158
01:24:59,522 --> 01:25:01,322
- Okay.
- Number two, an engineering major.

2159
01:25:01,322 --> 01:25:03,122
- An engineering major.
- An engineering major.

2160
01:25:03,252 --> 01:25:04,722
Number three, a young brain.

2161
01:25:04,722 --> 01:25:05,822
(Opponent candidate 3: A young brain)

2162
01:25:05,822 --> 01:25:07,062
They all sound formidable.

2163
01:25:07,062 --> 01:25:08,592
An engineering major has nothing to do with omok.

2164
01:25:08,592 --> 01:25:11,732
But out of the three, the engineering major sounds like...

2165
01:25:11,732 --> 01:25:12,862
the most formidable player.

2166
01:25:12,862 --> 01:25:15,832
I'm curious to see who the global leader is.

2167
01:25:16,202 --> 01:25:19,072
Can someone even play omok globally?

2168
01:25:19,642 --> 01:25:20,872
Don't you agree?

2169
01:25:20,872 --> 01:25:22,742
Who plays omok globally?

2170
01:25:22,742 --> 01:25:25,072
He's right. The global leader is probably the worst at it.

2171
01:25:25,072 --> 01:25:26,282
- The global leader...
- I'm curious.

2172
01:25:26,282 --> 01:25:27,382
- The global leader...
- Right.

2173
01:25:27,382 --> 01:25:29,082
The global leader is probably the worst at it.

2174
01:25:29,082 --> 01:25:30,512
Global?

2175
01:25:30,512 --> 01:25:32,082
What does that have to do with omok?

2176
01:25:32,582 --> 01:25:33,982
Just because someone is the UN Secretary-General...

2177
01:25:33,982 --> 01:25:35,392
doesn't mean he'll be good at playing omok.

2178
01:25:35,692 --> 01:25:37,392
- He's right.
- Yes. We'll go with global leader.

2179
01:25:37,392 --> 01:25:38,722
- Global leader.
- Global leader.

2180
01:25:38,722 --> 01:25:39,762
Okay.

2181
01:25:40,022 --> 01:25:41,892
- Come on out, global leader.
- Come on out.

2182
01:25:43,092 --> 01:25:44,262
- Gosh.
- Goodness.

2183
01:25:44,262 --> 01:25:47,702
(Who could the global leader be?)

2184
01:25:47,702 --> 01:25:49,972
- Jazz.
- I'm fine, thank you.

2185
01:25:49,972 --> 01:25:51,402
- Nice to meet you.
- Yes.

2186
01:25:51,402 --> 01:25:53,442
He went to the School of Global Leadership, Sungkyunkwan University.

2187
01:25:53,442 --> 01:25:54,702
(He's an alum of the School of Global Leadership.)

2188
01:25:54,942 --> 01:25:58,612
Have you ever lost an omok match?

2189
01:25:59,342 --> 01:26:00,512
I've only lost at omok…

2190
01:26:01,182 --> 01:26:02,352
a handful of times.

2191
01:26:03,612 --> 01:26:04,852
- He's a strong player.
- Gosh.

2192
01:26:05,252 --> 01:26:07,582
(His confidence took a sudden hit when a master player showed up.)

2193
01:26:07,582 --> 01:26:08,592
All right.

2194
01:26:09,452 --> 01:26:12,062
No, we can do this. Let's ride the luge.

2195
01:26:12,822 --> 01:26:13,862
You got this!

2196
01:26:13,862 --> 01:26:15,392
(You got this, son!)

2197
01:26:15,792 --> 01:26:17,892
(The players take their seats for the match.)

2198
01:26:17,892 --> 01:26:19,762
- You got this.
- With permanent markers?

2199
01:26:20,432 --> 01:26:21,872
(Representing the siblings, the luge fanatic)

2200
01:26:21,872 --> 01:26:23,732
(Representing the production staff, the global leader)

2201
01:26:24,032 --> 01:26:25,872
(Let the match begin.)

2202
01:26:25,872 --> 01:26:27,742
- The global leader.
- Are you taking a picture?

2203
01:26:29,742 --> 01:26:32,642
(You Seok plays Black and moves first.)

2204
01:26:33,342 --> 01:26:36,112
(The global leader plays White and catches up.)

2205
01:26:36,452 --> 01:26:38,052
- You can finish this quickly.
- Okay.

2206
01:26:38,052 --> 01:26:39,652
(Once the match starts, Sun Young cheers for You Seok.)

2207
01:26:40,022 --> 01:26:42,952
(Locked in)

2208
01:26:43,792 --> 01:26:44,792
You Seok.

2209
01:26:44,792 --> 01:26:46,922
(Black makes the second move.)

2210
01:26:47,322 --> 01:26:49,362
He won.

2211
01:26:50,192 --> 01:26:51,332
Was that a good move?

2212
01:26:53,032 --> 01:26:54,102
I'm not sure.

2213
01:26:54,532 --> 01:26:55,532
(Stunned)

2214
01:26:55,532 --> 01:26:56,632
- You don't know?
- No.

2215
01:26:56,632 --> 01:26:58,202
- I thought you knew.
- No.

2216
01:26:58,802 --> 01:27:00,372
I don't play omok like that.

2217
01:27:00,602 --> 01:27:02,672
- I play omok purely by instinct.
- I see.

2218
01:27:03,642 --> 01:27:06,442
(He's so locked in that he doesn't hear the cheering.)

2219
01:27:06,812 --> 01:27:08,912
(Just then,)

2220
01:27:08,982 --> 01:27:11,382
(You Seok suddenly picks up the pace.)

2221
01:27:12,122 --> 01:27:14,482
(What move did You Seok make?)

2222
01:27:15,652 --> 01:27:17,622
(He blocked White's advance...)

2223
01:27:17,792 --> 01:27:19,322
He has many options.

2224
01:27:19,322 --> 01:27:20,922
(while opening the way for Black.)

2225
01:27:21,422 --> 01:27:23,392
Good job. That was brilliant.

2226
01:27:25,032 --> 01:27:26,062
He's winning.

2227
01:27:26,062 --> 01:27:27,162
- He's winning?
- He's really winning.

2228
01:27:27,862 --> 01:27:30,402
I think seven moves should be enough.

2229
01:27:30,402 --> 01:27:32,202
(He's sure he can win within 7 moves.)

2230
01:27:32,542 --> 01:27:35,772
(You Seok's relentless attack continues.)

2231
01:27:36,372 --> 01:27:38,112
(Hesitating)

2232
01:27:39,512 --> 01:27:42,112
Are you sure he's good at this?

2233
01:27:42,112 --> 01:27:43,382
There are so many options.

2234
01:27:44,812 --> 01:27:46,282
Even an amateur like me can see there are many options.

2235
01:27:48,622 --> 01:27:49,692
It's over.

2236
01:27:49,692 --> 01:27:52,292
(It's over.)

2237
01:27:54,892 --> 01:27:57,192
- It's a 4-3, so he can't stop me.
- He can't stop you.

2238
01:27:57,192 --> 01:27:59,162
(Whatever move White makes, Black wins.)

2239
01:27:59,532 --> 01:28:01,762
Gosh, we won!

2240
01:28:01,762 --> 01:28:03,602
We won? Gosh.

2241
01:28:04,132 --> 01:28:08,402
(Filled with joy)

2242
01:28:08,402 --> 01:28:10,272
- You won?
- You really won.

2243
01:28:10,272 --> 01:28:12,482
- Gosh, you...
- You really are good at this.

2244
01:28:13,212 --> 01:28:15,012
- Gosh, it's hot.
- You won.

2245
01:28:15,012 --> 01:28:16,282
- You're good at this.
- My face got tanned.

2246
01:28:17,152 --> 01:28:18,482
Are we all set?

2247
01:28:18,482 --> 01:28:20,082
Wait, so does that mean we're going to ride the luge?

2248
01:28:20,682 --> 01:28:22,792
Why were you cheering for him to win...

2249
01:28:22,792 --> 01:28:24,022
if you don't want to ride the luge?

2250
01:28:24,022 --> 01:28:25,022
(I'm doomed.)

2251
01:28:25,252 --> 01:28:26,292
Thank you.

2252
01:28:26,292 --> 01:28:28,292
(He earned both the luge tickets and a boost of confidence.)

2253
01:28:28,292 --> 01:28:29,762
Great job.

2254
01:28:29,862 --> 01:28:31,032
- Great job.
- It's over.

2255
01:28:31,032 --> 01:28:32,062
Let's go.

2256
01:28:32,062 --> 01:28:34,062
(It's time to go grocery shopping.)

2257
01:28:34,062 --> 01:28:35,132
Let's go.

2258
01:28:35,132 --> 01:28:36,432
Good work, everyone.

2259
01:28:36,432 --> 01:28:38,102
- Good work, everyone.
- Good work, everyone.

2260
01:28:39,702 --> 01:28:41,872
Gosh, Jung Ah. I really struggled...

2261
01:28:41,872 --> 01:28:43,312
- with the teulitdae earlier.
- Right?

2262
01:28:43,412 --> 01:28:45,412
- We didn't have the technique.
- We really didn't.

2263
01:28:45,812 --> 01:28:48,082
It was so heavy. It was so heavy, we were wobbling.

2264
01:28:48,082 --> 01:28:50,582
- So much so that it felt dangerous.
- It did.

2265
01:28:50,582 --> 01:28:54,682
Yoon Seo really pushed through with sheer determination.

2266
01:28:54,682 --> 01:28:56,152
I basically used my face strength to turn it.

2267
01:28:56,852 --> 01:28:57,892
That's how I did it.

2268
01:28:57,892 --> 01:28:59,462
(She scrunched up her face, putting her whole body into it.)

2269
01:28:59,522 --> 01:29:01,662
You really worked hard.

2270
01:29:01,992 --> 01:29:03,032
(Embarrassed)

2271
01:29:03,032 --> 01:29:04,992
We're having a few drinks tonight.

2272
01:29:04,992 --> 01:29:07,232
- They provide everything.
- Even alcohol?

2273
01:29:07,232 --> 01:29:08,562
- It's Dajji.
- It's Dajji.

2274
01:29:08,562 --> 01:29:10,572
- I see.
- Unlimited drinks and alcohol.

2275
01:29:11,772 --> 01:29:13,202
(They're going to use the dining voucher...)

2276
01:29:13,202 --> 01:29:15,612
(they earned by harvesting sea squirts for Dajji.)

2277
01:29:15,742 --> 01:29:19,142
And If you want to go to karaoke, we can spend about 35 dollars.

2278
01:29:19,812 --> 01:29:22,952
I'm fine singing if it's just us,

2279
01:29:22,952 --> 01:29:25,082
but I feel embarrassed about to do it on TV.

2280
01:29:25,282 --> 01:29:26,682
I'm not a good singer.

2281
01:29:27,022 --> 01:29:28,792
I get too nervous to enjoy singing.

2282
01:29:29,222 --> 01:29:31,792
I don't think the viewers are expecting much.

2283
01:29:31,792 --> 01:29:33,622
I know they're not,

2284
01:29:33,622 --> 01:29:35,632
but I'm still embarrassed because I'm bad at it.

2285
01:29:35,632 --> 01:29:37,562
- "They're not expecting much."
- I don't feel confident.

2286
01:29:38,432 --> 01:29:41,032
(Flustered)

2287
01:29:41,202 --> 01:29:42,532
What do you want to do?

2288
01:29:42,532 --> 01:29:45,702
Are you really trying to think about the viewers?

2289
01:29:46,272 --> 01:29:47,772
If you want what's best for the viewers...

2290
01:29:47,772 --> 01:29:50,542
You have to sing, even if you can't.

2291
01:29:50,872 --> 01:29:52,282
Hae Joon, when you go to karaoke,

2292
01:29:52,282 --> 01:29:53,882
what kind of songs do you sing?

2293
01:29:54,012 --> 01:29:55,952
I'm more of a technical singer.

2294
01:29:55,952 --> 01:29:57,852
What? You use a lot of vocal techniques?

2295
01:29:58,852 --> 01:30:00,982
Gosh, that's probably pretty tiring to listen to...

2296
01:30:01,052 --> 01:30:02,492
after a few songs. Right?

2297
01:30:02,952 --> 01:30:05,692
(Looking forward to Hae Joon's vocal techniques at karaoke)

2298
01:30:05,992 --> 01:30:09,932
I should think about the ingredients I'll need for the curry.

2299
01:30:10,292 --> 01:30:13,602
Well, curry is...

2300
01:30:14,032 --> 01:30:15,332
You Seok...

2301
01:30:16,002 --> 01:30:17,802
said he has his own special recipe for curry.

2302
01:30:17,802 --> 01:30:19,242
- Really?
- He said it's a secret.

2303
01:30:19,472 --> 01:30:20,602
(Thinking)

2304
01:30:20,602 --> 01:30:23,612
Jung Ah, how do you feel about MSG?

2305
01:30:24,072 --> 01:30:26,412
It's fine if it tastes good.

2306
01:30:26,682 --> 01:30:29,052
We'll buy a packet of beef seasoning powder.

2307
01:30:29,052 --> 01:30:30,452
(We'll add some MSG.)

2308
01:30:30,782 --> 01:30:32,622
You're putting beef seasoning powder in curry?

2309
01:30:32,752 --> 01:30:35,222
I guess cooking is about technique.

2310
01:30:35,522 --> 01:30:37,952
I think he might have too many techniques for everything.

2311
01:30:38,452 --> 01:30:40,362
Have you heard of Park Poong?

2312
01:30:41,222 --> 01:30:42,632
(Poong as in Kim Poong, writer and master of fusion cuisine)

2313
01:30:42,792 --> 01:30:43,992
Since we're in Tongyeong,

2314
01:30:44,592 --> 01:30:46,802
we should make Tongyeong-style curry.

2315
01:30:46,802 --> 01:30:47,832
Really?

2316
01:30:47,832 --> 01:30:50,132
- With seaweed and sea squirt?
- Yes.

2317
01:30:50,132 --> 01:30:51,472
We should use seaweed and sea squirt.

2318
01:30:52,142 --> 01:30:53,502
- Seriously?
- Of course.

2319
01:30:53,602 --> 01:30:55,372
Seaweed and sea squirt in curry?

2320
01:30:55,372 --> 01:30:56,472
They might not go well with curry.

2321
01:30:56,612 --> 01:30:59,812
He wants to come in last.

2322
01:30:59,812 --> 01:31:01,212
We were here yesterday.

2323
01:31:01,212 --> 01:31:03,252
(They arrived at the supermarket while talking about curry.)

2324
01:31:03,582 --> 01:31:05,782
I'll wait in the car while you get groceries.

2325
01:31:06,722 --> 01:31:08,182
- You're not going with us?
- No.

2326
01:31:08,422 --> 01:31:10,292
Because I shouldn't see the ingredients you get.

2327
01:31:10,852 --> 01:31:14,622
(The contestants begin grocery shopping.)

2328
01:31:14,892 --> 01:31:17,462
(Park Poong heads straight to the fridge.)

2329
01:31:17,592 --> 01:31:18,862
- Hae Joon.
- Yes?

2330
01:31:18,862 --> 01:31:21,132
- How many...
- Why did I get so startled?

2331
01:31:21,502 --> 01:31:23,432
- How many carrots do you need?
- Only about half a carrot.

2332
01:31:23,432 --> 01:31:25,032
Right? Then I should get one more.

2333
01:31:26,042 --> 01:31:27,142
Goodness.

2334
01:31:27,802 --> 01:31:29,542
(Cautious)

2335
01:31:29,542 --> 01:31:33,842
(He quietly picks up a pack of tomatoes.)

2336
01:31:34,942 --> 01:31:36,712
He's using one, and I'm using half.

2337
01:31:36,712 --> 01:31:37,782
(Glancing at Sun Young)

2338
01:31:38,482 --> 01:31:40,182
Potatoes. Should we get one more?

2339
01:31:40,582 --> 01:31:42,922
It's getting intense.

2340
01:31:43,092 --> 01:31:45,222
Of course.

2341
01:31:45,392 --> 01:31:46,992
Who put these tomatoes in here?

2342
01:31:47,192 --> 01:31:48,932
The tomatoes? I wanted to eat some.

2343
01:31:48,932 --> 01:31:51,392
You wanted to eat some? Can I have one too?

2344
01:31:51,392 --> 01:31:53,402
For your curry or to eat?

2345
01:31:53,402 --> 01:31:55,132
- For my curry.
- Gosh.

2346
01:31:55,132 --> 01:31:56,302
(Feeling deflated)

2347
01:31:56,632 --> 01:31:57,932
(His secret ingredient was immediately discovered.)

2348
01:31:57,932 --> 01:32:00,472
- Should we get another pack?
- No, I don't need that many.

2349
01:32:00,472 --> 01:32:01,872
- I'm just going to use one.
- Who put the tomatoes in there?

2350
01:32:01,872 --> 01:32:03,412
- Me.
- Potatoes, carrots, onions. And?

2351
01:32:03,412 --> 01:32:05,372
- Are you putting in tomatoes?
- I'm doing it too.

2352
01:32:05,372 --> 01:32:06,582
I was going to do that.

2353
01:32:07,982 --> 01:32:08,982
We're all using tomatoes?

2354
01:32:08,982 --> 01:32:10,582
Gosh, this can't be happening.

2355
01:32:10,582 --> 01:32:11,652
was going to sneak some tomatoes into the cart.

2356
01:32:11,652 --> 01:32:13,752
- You thought of tomatoes?
- Tomato paste.

2357
01:32:13,852 --> 01:32:16,092
I was going to put in tomato paste.

2358
01:32:16,092 --> 01:32:18,192
Paste? Why don't you just make yourself ramyeon?

2359
01:32:19,592 --> 01:32:22,432
Tomato paste is just seasoned tomatoes.

2360
01:32:22,832 --> 01:32:24,232
Then why not just buy pre-made curry?

2361
01:32:24,232 --> 01:32:25,232
Let's each shop for our own ingredients.

2362
01:32:25,232 --> 01:32:26,232
(Grumbling)

2363
01:32:26,962 --> 01:32:28,702
(Thinking)

2364
01:32:30,232 --> 01:32:31,602
I'm going to hide this in my pocket...

2365
01:32:31,602 --> 01:32:33,102
and take it out at the register.

2366
01:32:34,172 --> 01:32:35,812
(Hiding)

2367
01:32:37,512 --> 01:32:38,612
(Spying)

2368
01:32:38,612 --> 01:32:39,812
What? Hey.

2369
01:32:40,312 --> 01:32:41,442
Then I'm doomed.

2370
01:32:41,442 --> 01:32:43,282
(Her plans fall apart because she can't find what she wanted.)

2371
01:32:43,282 --> 01:32:45,282
The brand I usually use...

2372
01:32:45,982 --> 01:32:48,222
Let's go get some ice cream.

2373
01:32:48,822 --> 01:32:49,952
- What?
- Nothing.

2374
01:32:50,222 --> 01:32:52,022
- Why are you being so secretive?
- You go ahead.

2375
01:32:52,662 --> 01:32:55,062
Excuse me, ma'am. Where can I find chicken stock?

2376
01:32:55,062 --> 01:32:56,132
- Pardon?
- Chicken stock.

2377
01:32:56,132 --> 01:32:57,732
You can just point me in the direction.

2378
01:32:57,992 --> 01:32:59,102
This middle section?

2379
01:32:59,702 --> 01:33:01,162
Why do you keep looking, Sun Young?

2380
01:33:01,162 --> 01:33:02,672
I'm not going to copy your ingredients.

2381
01:33:03,832 --> 01:33:07,442
Chefs, the curry showdown is about to begin.

2382
01:33:07,442 --> 01:33:09,642
(Fresh Curry Arena)

2383
01:33:09,642 --> 01:33:12,812
Welcome to the Fresh Curry Arena.

2384
01:33:14,312 --> 01:33:17,312
(The perfect setting for the curry showdown)

2385
01:33:17,452 --> 01:33:18,552
She's here.

2386
01:33:19,282 --> 01:33:20,552
- Gosh, she looks pretty.
- Satisfy Master Yum Jung Ah's...

2387
01:33:20,552 --> 01:33:22,792
- Hello.
- taste buds.

2388
01:33:23,992 --> 01:33:25,792
Let's begin the curry showdown.

2389
01:33:27,162 --> 01:33:28,892
My goal is to make sure it turns out well.

2390
01:33:28,892 --> 01:33:30,792
(Roh Yoon Seo: My goal is to finish it in time.)

2391
01:33:31,062 --> 01:33:32,632
If I don't come first, who will?

2392
01:33:32,732 --> 01:33:33,862
I'm going to win this, no matter what.

2393
01:33:34,502 --> 01:33:36,302
I'm going to make that 90s-style curry...

2394
01:33:36,632 --> 01:33:38,202
that we grew up eating.

2395
01:33:38,472 --> 01:33:40,302
I want to make something different.

2396
01:33:40,302 --> 01:33:41,642
(Cooking skills: Unable to determine)

2397
01:33:42,072 --> 01:33:45,012
(The four chefs go head-to-head to become the ultimate curry legend.)

2398
01:33:45,572 --> 01:33:49,082
(Out of the four different curries,)

2399
01:33:49,582 --> 01:33:51,912
(which one will win over...)

2400
01:33:52,252 --> 01:33:54,322
(Master Yum Jung Ah?)

2401
01:33:54,752 --> 01:33:57,052
Coming soon, the siblings' curry showdown.

2402
01:33:58,352 --> 01:34:01,422
(After the intense grocery shopping)

2403
01:34:01,422 --> 01:34:03,062
- Now that we've started, - You guys are so funny.

2404
01:34:03,062 --> 01:34:04,992
- it's a full-on battle.
- Is it?

2405
01:34:05,432 --> 01:34:07,902
We were in there trying to hide what we were picking out from each other.

2406
01:34:08,362 --> 01:34:11,102
Everyone's using all kinds of ingredients, including fruits.

2407
01:34:11,102 --> 01:34:12,172
It's so interesting.

2408
01:34:12,472 --> 01:34:14,302
- You Seok.
- Yes?

2409
01:34:14,302 --> 01:34:15,402
You're amazing.

2410
01:34:15,872 --> 01:34:17,572
- Why?
- You got your wish.

2411
01:34:18,042 --> 01:34:19,682
- I'm so happy.
- The luge.

2412
01:34:20,312 --> 01:34:21,782
No one else wanted to do it,

2413
01:34:22,042 --> 01:34:24,152
but you got your wish.

2414
01:34:24,882 --> 01:34:27,122
- Gosh.
- We're being led around by him.

2415
01:34:27,122 --> 01:34:28,182
Yes.

2416
01:34:28,422 --> 01:34:32,122
(Magnet Kang, actor: Leads the siblings around)

2417
01:34:32,792 --> 01:34:35,322
Gosh, You Seok. You have so many things you want to do.

2418
01:34:35,622 --> 01:34:36,992
- This vibe.
- Yes.

2419
01:34:36,992 --> 01:34:38,232
Houses tucked away in every little alley.

2420
01:34:38,232 --> 01:34:39,232
(They arrive at the village.)

2421
01:34:40,232 --> 01:34:41,662
I see the house.

2422
01:34:42,262 --> 01:34:43,302
Those are our bikes.

2423
01:34:43,302 --> 01:34:44,402
(After an uphill walk, they finally reach the Siblings' House.)

2424
01:34:44,402 --> 01:34:45,632
- You have bikes?
- Yes.

2425
01:34:45,872 --> 01:34:47,572
Welcome to the Siblings' House.

2426
01:34:47,572 --> 01:34:48,702
Ta-da!

2427
01:34:49,142 --> 01:34:50,212
Gosh, it's pretty.

2428
01:34:50,312 --> 01:34:52,782
(In awe)

2429
01:34:53,312 --> 01:34:54,582
Look at the flowers!

2430
01:34:54,582 --> 01:34:55,782
(Hae Joon, look at the flowers!)

2431
01:34:55,982 --> 01:34:58,912
(The yard is overflowing with peonies in bloom.)

2432
01:34:59,652 --> 01:35:02,352
Gosh, this house is so nice.

2433
01:35:04,892 --> 01:35:06,662
There's a vegetable garden here.

2434
01:35:07,662 --> 01:35:09,262
(Hae Joon is pleased to see...)

2435
01:35:09,262 --> 01:35:10,932
(the small vegetable garden on the roof.)

2436
01:35:11,892 --> 01:35:14,802
It would be nice to come up here at night and have a beer.

2437
01:35:15,732 --> 01:35:17,732
- Isn't it nice?
- It is.

2438
01:35:18,832 --> 01:35:21,442
(A simple, heartfelt remark)

2439
01:35:21,942 --> 01:35:22,942
I love Tongyeong.

2440
01:35:24,812 --> 01:35:25,882
I love Tongyeong.

2441
01:35:26,842 --> 01:35:28,482
I'm going to sleep like a baby tonight.

2442
01:35:28,582 --> 01:35:30,212
I can sleep like a baby right now.

2443
01:35:31,552 --> 01:35:32,752
- Let's take a break.
- Yes.

2444
01:35:32,752 --> 01:35:33,822
- Let's take a break.
- Let's relax a bit.

2445
01:35:33,822 --> 01:35:34,882
(The siblings decide to take a break.)

2446
01:35:34,982 --> 01:35:37,592
(While Sun Young and You Seok lie down and rest,)

2447
01:35:38,022 --> 01:35:39,462
(Jung Ah and Yoon Seo are freshening up.)

2448
01:35:39,862 --> 01:35:41,492
Do you want me to do your hair?

2449
01:35:41,992 --> 01:35:43,992
Right now? You think you can do it?

2450
01:35:44,332 --> 01:35:46,632
If I try and fail, we'll just have to...

2451
01:35:46,632 --> 01:35:47,762
Just braid it like this.

2452
01:35:49,202 --> 01:35:51,802
(Art school graduate Yoon Seo opens her magical hair salon.)

2453
01:35:52,032 --> 01:35:55,502
(She's clearly nervous about her first customer.)

2454
01:35:55,772 --> 01:35:58,442
(With steady hands, she begins braiding Jung Ah's hair.)

2455
01:35:59,542 --> 01:36:01,182
It's cool that you know how to do this.

2456
01:36:02,342 --> 01:36:03,382
This is my first time.

2457
01:36:04,752 --> 01:36:06,822
- Did you watch a YouTube tutorial?
- I did.

2458
01:36:08,582 --> 01:36:11,152
- I'm not sure I can do a good job.
- It's okay. Don't worry about it.

2459
01:36:11,992 --> 01:36:13,622
I'm starting to see the shape of it.

2460
01:36:14,262 --> 01:36:16,532
My hair has gone flat...

2461
01:36:16,732 --> 01:36:18,062
from wearing a hat all day.

2462
01:36:18,432 --> 01:36:20,702
Are you braiding it for a ponytail?

2463
01:36:20,702 --> 01:36:22,402
Do you want a ponytail or pigtails?

2464
01:36:22,572 --> 01:36:24,802
I can't wear pigtails in Seoul, so I wanted to try them here.

2465
01:36:25,232 --> 01:36:26,502
- I get what you mean.
- Right?

2466
01:36:26,502 --> 01:36:27,772
When you're travelling,

2467
01:36:28,072 --> 01:36:29,212
you become more adventurous with your style.

2468
01:36:29,472 --> 01:36:32,142
(Yoon Seo continues to braid Jung Ah's hair while they talk.)

2469
01:36:32,942 --> 01:36:33,982
(Like a bird)

2470
01:36:35,042 --> 01:36:36,982
(They hear someone singing outside their room.)

2471
01:36:37,752 --> 01:36:38,752
Hae Joon's having fun.

2472
01:36:40,552 --> 01:36:43,352
(The only thing I can give you)

2473
01:36:44,252 --> 01:36:46,822
(He is captivated by the record player in the living room.)

2474
01:36:47,992 --> 01:36:50,332
(Is my love)

2475
01:36:52,092 --> 01:36:55,162
(He puts a carefully selected vinyl on the record player.)

2476
01:36:56,202 --> 01:36:57,402
We have to listen to this song. It's a classic.

2477
01:36:57,402 --> 01:36:58,432
What is it?

2478
01:36:59,472 --> 01:37:02,472
(Hae Joon turns up the volume.)

2479
01:37:04,242 --> 01:37:08,312
(The song has a very nostalgic feel.)

2480
01:37:08,782 --> 01:37:10,552
It's a government-sponsored morality song.

2481
01:37:11,082 --> 01:37:12,682
(A genre of songs promoted after the Japanese colonial period...)

2482
01:37:12,682 --> 01:37:14,952
(that carried messages of social education and moral instruction)

2483
01:37:14,952 --> 01:37:16,752
Every album was required to include at least one by law.

2484
01:37:16,992 --> 01:37:19,692
("Uh-hoya Dunggidunggi" by Lee Moon Se)

2485
01:37:19,962 --> 01:37:24,932
(Let's come together and share)

2486
01:37:24,932 --> 01:37:28,162
(Both the joys and the hardships)

2487
01:37:28,402 --> 01:37:32,542
(We're all familiar neighbours)

2488
01:37:32,542 --> 01:37:36,612
(Like one big family)

2489
01:37:36,942 --> 01:37:40,582
(A place full of warmth)

2490
01:37:40,582 --> 01:37:44,152
(Our village, a village of flowers)

2491
01:37:44,712 --> 01:37:48,052
(Wistful)

2492
01:37:48,682 --> 01:37:50,722
Listening to it now,

2493
01:37:51,322 --> 01:37:52,622
he actually sang it really well.

2494
01:37:53,522 --> 01:37:54,592
He's like my dad.

2495
01:37:54,592 --> 01:37:55,962
(Giggling)

2496
01:37:56,762 --> 01:37:59,962
(Hae Joon sat there listening to old songs for a while.)

2497
01:38:00,662 --> 01:38:01,762
I look like a young lady from the Joseon dynasty.

2498
01:38:01,762 --> 01:38:04,732
- You look so elegant.
- I look like a young lady.

2499
01:38:05,602 --> 01:38:08,102
Your hair looks like it was styled by a professional.

2500
01:38:08,172 --> 01:38:10,872
(Salon Director Roh is proud.)

2501
01:38:11,212 --> 01:38:14,112
(This guy looks like he was styled by a professional too.)

2502
01:38:15,782 --> 01:38:16,782
(Looking cool)

2503
01:38:17,552 --> 01:38:19,012
(Laughing)

2504
01:38:19,522 --> 01:38:21,982
- You really went all out.
- Why are you laughing?

2505
01:38:21,982 --> 01:38:23,022
You really dressed up.

2506
01:38:23,022 --> 01:38:24,352
- You're really dressed up.
- You told me to dress up.

2507
01:38:25,252 --> 01:38:27,892
(Captain Yum thinks it cute to see You Seok all dressed up.)

2508
01:38:28,162 --> 01:38:29,632
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

2509
01:38:30,062 --> 01:38:32,562
- Let's go before they close.
- Okay.

2510
01:38:32,562 --> 01:38:33,802
(Let's make You Seok's dream of riding a luge together come true!)

2511
01:38:34,202 --> 01:38:36,172
As long as You Seok's happy.

2512
01:38:36,472 --> 01:38:39,402
Of course, that's why I'm even going.

2513
01:38:39,402 --> 01:38:41,672
Why are you so eager to ride it?

2514
01:38:41,942 --> 01:38:44,112
When else would I get the chance to come to Tongyeong...

2515
01:38:44,112 --> 01:38:47,082
with my older sisters, my older brother,

2516
01:38:47,082 --> 01:38:48,582
and my younger sister, and go luge riding together?

2517
01:38:48,582 --> 01:38:50,112
(If not now, when?)

2518
01:38:51,152 --> 01:38:53,822
- Goodness.
- Goodness.

2519
01:38:55,122 --> 01:38:56,652
We only get this moment once.

2520
01:38:58,652 --> 01:38:59,692
He's much more articulate now.

2521
01:39:00,962 --> 01:39:01,962
What a smooth talker.

2522
01:39:02,422 --> 01:39:04,662
- The way he worded that.
- Let's live in the moment.

2523
01:39:04,662 --> 01:39:06,532
- Goodness. Carpe diem?
- Carpe diem.

2524
