(Humming)

2773
01:48:36,402 --> 01:48:37,972
(A taste that makes your eyes widen)

2774
01:48:37,972 --> 01:48:39,002
It's good.

2775
01:48:40,572 --> 01:48:42,142
Don't we just eat this?

2776
01:48:42,142 --> 01:48:43,642
- Of course.
- Have some rice.

2777
01:48:43,642 --> 01:48:45,072
- My gosh.
- We worked hard today.

2778
01:48:45,072 --> 01:48:46,582
- The raw fish is incredible.
- Eat a lot.

2779
01:48:46,582 --> 01:48:48,642
- Is the raw fish excellent?
- It's very fresh.

2780
01:48:49,042 --> 01:48:50,552
- Enjoy the food.
- It's very fresh.

2781
01:48:50,852 --> 01:48:53,082
- Isn't the raw fish amazing?
- Yes.

2782
01:48:53,112 --> 01:48:54,152
Sea squirt.

2783
01:48:54,282 --> 01:48:55,482
- I'll eat it as much as I want.
- Because of work...

2784
01:48:55,482 --> 01:48:56,652
I know.

2785
01:48:56,692 --> 01:48:58,352
Do you eat on time?

2786
01:48:59,192 --> 01:49:01,722
(Pulling out the murex from the shell)

2787
01:49:02,462 --> 01:49:05,392
(Gobbling it up neatly)

2788
01:49:05,932 --> 01:49:07,632
Gosh, this is nice.

2789
01:49:09,002 --> 01:49:10,572
It seems like the middle-aged man showed up for a moment.

2790
01:49:11,532 --> 01:49:12,572
It happens sometimes.

2791
01:49:14,202 --> 01:49:18,242
(This is the seafood paradise, and Mr. Kang is in love with it.)

2792
01:49:18,442 --> 01:49:19,772
- It's baby octopus.
- Try it...

2793
01:49:19,772 --> 01:49:21,012
in a wrap.

2794
01:49:21,012 --> 01:49:22,942
- Isn't the baby octopus tasty?
- Yes.

2795
01:49:24,552 --> 01:49:25,652
How does it taste?

2796
01:49:26,582 --> 01:49:28,482
It tastes like squid.

2797
01:49:28,482 --> 01:49:29,722
- Does it taste like squid?
- Yes.

2798
01:49:29,722 --> 01:49:30,922
- Then it must be good.
- Yes.

2799
01:49:30,922 --> 01:49:33,192
- Sea squirt...
- Because of the eyes...

2800
01:49:33,192 --> 01:49:34,292
Right.

2801
01:49:34,292 --> 01:49:36,292
It has eyes. We made eye contact.

2802
01:49:36,292 --> 01:49:37,392
(Bright-eyed)

2803
01:49:37,392 --> 01:49:38,462
- You made eye contact?
- Yes.

2804
01:49:38,462 --> 01:49:40,002
Does it have a mouth?

2805
01:49:40,502 --> 01:49:42,002
- It has a mouth.
- You don't feel it?

2806
01:49:42,702 --> 01:49:44,502
I can feel all of them. The eyes, the nose, and the mouth.

2807
01:49:44,502 --> 01:49:45,502
My goodness.

2808
01:49:45,502 --> 01:49:47,872
(Your eyes, nose, mouth)

2809
01:49:47,872 --> 01:49:50,642
(Dancing)

2810
01:49:50,812 --> 01:49:51,942
(Eating out even makes Captain Yum dance.)

2811
01:49:51,942 --> 01:49:53,512
Now that everyone had a drink...

2812
01:49:53,942 --> 01:49:55,512
My goodness.

2813
01:49:56,142 --> 01:49:57,552
All right.

2814
01:49:57,652 --> 01:49:59,552
After the meal, everyone should get some rest.

2815
01:50:00,282 --> 01:50:01,452
Aren't you our guest?

2816
01:50:02,722 --> 01:50:04,022
You sound like the host.

2817
01:50:04,022 --> 01:50:05,892
(People might think that he's the host.)

2818
01:50:06,762 --> 01:50:09,162
(The younger ones are peeling the shrimp diligently.)

2819
01:50:09,762 --> 01:50:11,262
What do you think about the shrimp debate?

2820
01:50:11,762 --> 01:50:13,532
The shrimp debate? What about it?

2821
01:50:13,732 --> 01:50:15,232
What's the shrimp debate?

2822
01:50:15,232 --> 01:50:16,602
(The shrimp debate?)

2823
01:50:16,672 --> 01:50:18,102
- It's...
- It's like the perilla leaf debate.

2824
01:50:18,102 --> 01:50:19,502
- Right.
- It's like the perilla leaf debate.

2825
01:50:19,502 --> 01:50:22,672
It's about peeling shrimp for your partner's friend...

2826
01:50:22,672 --> 01:50:23,812
of the opposite sex.

2827
01:50:24,242 --> 01:50:26,272
(If your partner peels shrimp for another person...)

2828
01:50:26,272 --> 01:50:28,882
(of the opposite sex, is that okay or not?)

2829
01:50:28,942 --> 01:50:29,982
- Right.
- Oh, my.

2830
01:50:30,182 --> 01:50:32,612
- You mean, my husband?
- Yes.

2831
01:50:33,082 --> 01:50:34,552
- For example...
- Why would he?

2832
01:50:34,552 --> 01:50:36,482
- Doesn't she have any fingers?
- My husband peels shrimp...

2833
01:50:36,522 --> 01:50:37,522
(Shaking)

2834
01:50:37,522 --> 01:50:38,922
- "Fingers?"
- My husband peels shrimp...

2835
01:50:38,922 --> 01:50:40,092
for another woman?

2836
01:50:40,762 --> 01:50:41,822
So...

2837
01:50:41,822 --> 01:50:42,962
Why would you peel that for her?

2838
01:50:44,062 --> 01:50:45,262
I didn't.

2839
01:50:47,002 --> 01:50:48,462
That's not okay.

2840
01:50:48,462 --> 01:50:50,102
Why would he do something like that?

2841
01:50:50,772 --> 01:50:52,332
That's totally unnecessary.

2842
01:50:52,402 --> 01:50:53,742
What do you think?

2843
01:50:55,442 --> 01:50:57,042
I don't really care.

2844
01:50:57,042 --> 01:50:58,642
If someone wants to do it, they can.

2845
01:50:59,112 --> 01:51:01,982
(What did you say?)

2846
01:51:01,982 --> 01:51:05,212
- If someone doesn't want to...
- Let's say your wife is...

2847
01:51:05,552 --> 01:51:09,322
sitting across the table a little far from you.

2848
01:51:09,322 --> 01:51:12,752
She starts peeling shrimp for a male friend...

2849
01:51:12,752 --> 01:51:14,092
- Your male friends.
- sitting in front of her.

2850
01:51:14,092 --> 01:51:15,762
- A man is peeling it?
- No, for a man.

2851
01:51:16,792 --> 01:51:18,462
It depends on who that man is.

2852
01:51:18,462 --> 01:51:20,502
He's very similar to you.

2853
01:51:20,662 --> 01:51:22,632
- He makes more money than you, - Goodness.

2854
01:51:23,472 --> 01:51:25,302
and he's more handsome than you.

2855
01:51:26,172 --> 01:51:28,172
It's someone you'd find impressive.

2856
01:51:28,172 --> 01:51:30,372
- Someone I'd feel jealous of?
- Yes.

2857
01:51:30,372 --> 01:51:31,442
- So what do you think?
- Gosh.

2858
01:51:32,342 --> 01:51:34,082
- You wouldn't be okay, right?
- I wouldn't be okay.

2859
01:51:34,712 --> 01:51:37,112
He shook his head about four times.

2860
01:51:37,112 --> 01:51:38,712
- That's not okay.
- It's not okay.

2861
01:51:38,712 --> 01:51:40,222
- Of course not.
- It's not okay.

2862
01:51:40,982 --> 01:51:41,982
More food is coming.

2863
01:51:42,182 --> 01:51:43,222
- More?
- Yes.

2864
01:51:43,222 --> 01:51:44,852
You brought it at the perfect time.

2865
01:51:44,852 --> 01:51:46,392
This is the last one this year.

2866
01:51:46,392 --> 01:51:47,422
Really?

2867
01:51:47,422 --> 01:51:49,392
- What is it?
- It'll be available next spring...

2868
01:51:49,392 --> 01:51:52,462
- when azaleas bloom.
- It's azaleas.

2869
01:51:52,462 --> 01:51:53,462
(Flower jeon made with azaleas)

2870
01:51:53,462 --> 01:51:55,462
- That's fascinating.
- Is it made with glutinous rice?

2871
01:51:55,462 --> 01:51:57,802
- Yes, it's glutinous rice.
- So that's why.

2872
01:51:57,802 --> 01:51:58,972
It looks very unusual.

2873
01:51:59,072 --> 01:52:00,402
- By the way...
- I've never had it before.

2874
01:52:00,572 --> 01:52:02,842
Jeon is often made with glutinous rice in Gyeongsang Province.

2875
01:52:03,002 --> 01:52:05,042
- It's like rice cakes.
- I agree.

2876
01:52:06,882 --> 01:52:07,882
(Everyone is savouring the azalea jeon together.)

2877
01:52:07,882 --> 01:52:09,782
- It's very unique.
- I love this.

2878
01:52:09,782 --> 01:52:11,082
It's my kind of style.

2879
01:52:11,312 --> 01:52:13,582
Gyeongsang Province style.

2880
01:52:13,582 --> 01:52:14,922
- Yes.
- It's like rice cakes.

2881
01:52:14,922 --> 01:52:16,722
- I haven't had this in a long time.
- Me neither.

2882
01:52:16,722 --> 01:52:18,522
- My mom used to make it for me.
- Exactly.

2883
01:52:18,522 --> 01:52:20,122
- Do you usually make this at home?
- Yes.

2884
01:52:20,122 --> 01:52:21,422
- At home, - I haven't tasted this...

2885
01:52:21,422 --> 01:52:22,562
- in a very long time.
- we made it this small.

2886
01:52:22,562 --> 01:52:24,062
We made it this small with a lot of oil.

2887
01:52:24,062 --> 01:52:26,262
This one is big, but my mom made it this small...

2888
01:52:26,262 --> 01:52:27,762
in several pieces.

2889
01:52:27,932 --> 01:52:29,032
- The taste of home.
- Are these azaleas?

2890
01:52:29,032 --> 01:52:30,202
Yes.

2891
01:52:30,202 --> 01:52:31,602
(Jeon made with his mother's love)

2892
01:52:31,602 --> 01:52:32,932
I see.

2893
01:52:32,932 --> 01:52:33,942
It's like hotteok.

2894
01:52:33,942 --> 01:52:35,572
- We eat it like this.
- It's so good.

2895
01:52:35,572 --> 01:52:36,642
(You find both flavours and memories at Dajji.)

2896
01:52:36,642 --> 01:52:38,672
Suddenly, there was a strong gust of wind.

2897
01:52:38,672 --> 01:52:40,712
The boat started rocking,

2898
01:52:40,712 --> 01:52:43,552
and the ladies in the back screamed.

2899
01:52:43,552 --> 01:52:45,452
How do you know? Did the captain tell you?

2900
01:52:45,452 --> 01:52:47,852
- He told me about it.
- Did he tell you?

2901
01:52:47,852 --> 01:52:49,382
Pretty ladies screamed and everything.

2902
01:52:49,382 --> 01:52:51,152
He's so silly.

2903
01:52:51,152 --> 01:52:52,152
(You Seok tells the story of the outboard boat.)

2904
01:52:53,722 --> 01:52:54,992
I want to go fishing.

2905
01:52:56,022 --> 01:52:57,192
I want to go fishing.

2906
01:53:00,132 --> 01:53:02,162
What if we go fishing and catch something?

2907
01:53:02,162 --> 01:53:03,402
(Eyes closing tightly)

2908
01:53:03,932 --> 01:53:05,532
- I don't think it's a good idea.
- You're driving me crazy.

2909
01:53:05,532 --> 01:53:06,872
Jung Ah, I don't like it either.

2910
01:53:06,872 --> 01:53:09,302
- I keep making things bigger...
- It's a bad idea.

2911
01:53:09,302 --> 01:53:10,412
- than they need to be.
- This isn't it.

2912
01:53:10,412 --> 01:53:11,772
I'm afraid that Jung Ah will hate me.

2913
01:53:11,772 --> 01:53:13,942
So I'll stop taking on big projects.

2914
01:53:14,442 --> 01:53:16,682
What I want to do is very important.

2915
01:53:16,682 --> 01:53:18,112
Then you can go fishing alone.

2916
01:53:18,112 --> 01:53:19,282
- So...
- You can go...

2917
01:53:19,282 --> 01:53:21,182
I won't take you with me.

2918
01:53:21,322 --> 01:53:23,182
- I'm not going.
- I'll go fishing alone.

2919
01:53:23,182 --> 01:53:24,552
I'll make breakfast,

2920
01:53:24,552 --> 01:53:25,852
- so you and Hae Joon can go.
- We'll go and catch fish.

2921
01:53:25,852 --> 01:53:27,262
- We'll make breakfast.
- And we'll go fishing.

2922
01:53:27,262 --> 01:53:28,592
- Good luck.
- We'll make breakfast instead.

2923
01:53:28,592 --> 01:53:30,062
- I won't take you with me.
- Okay.

2924
01:53:30,062 --> 01:53:31,092
I feel more comfortable on the boat.

2925
01:53:31,092 --> 01:53:33,362
- Father.
- Gosh, spicy fish stew is served.

2926
01:53:33,362 --> 01:53:34,702
- Father.
- Yes?

2927
01:53:35,262 --> 01:53:36,262
Three things tomorrow...

2928
01:53:36,262 --> 01:53:37,572
- Running, - Okay.

2929
01:53:37,572 --> 01:53:38,932
cycling, or a boat ride.

2930
01:53:38,932 --> 01:53:40,472
Which do you want to do the most?

2931
01:53:40,842 --> 01:53:43,372
Which is the best? Running is the easiest.

2932
01:53:43,372 --> 01:53:44,772
- Running?
- Yes, it's the easiest.

2933
01:53:45,912 --> 01:53:47,012
You don't want to go on a boat?

2934
01:53:47,312 --> 01:53:48,942
What would we do on a boat?

2935
01:53:49,212 --> 01:53:51,812
(It's a story we've heard before.)

2936
01:53:51,812 --> 01:53:53,152
He fell for it.

2937
01:53:53,152 --> 01:53:55,552
- He got caught.
- He'll end up on the boat anyway.

2938
01:53:55,552 --> 01:53:57,352
- Right. Whatever You Seok says...
- Jung Ah.

2939
01:53:57,352 --> 01:53:59,792
- comes true.
- He'll end up on the boat.

2940
01:53:59,792 --> 01:54:01,162
- Jung Ah.
- Whatever he says...

2941
01:54:01,162 --> 01:54:03,632
- comes true.
- We'll only look at the outcome.

2942
01:54:03,632 --> 01:54:05,162
Weren't you on a boat today?

2943
01:54:06,362 --> 01:54:07,632
But you weren't.

2944
01:54:07,702 --> 01:54:09,432
He's crazy about boats.

2945
01:54:10,172 --> 01:54:12,372
- But I'm scared of...
- I told you not to get on the boat!

2946
01:54:14,572 --> 01:54:18,412
(Suddenly, he turns into Yang Gwan Sik.)

2947
01:54:18,412 --> 01:54:21,382
- "I told you not to get on it."
- You're meant to ride the boat.

2948
01:54:21,382 --> 01:54:22,542
He was meant to?

2949
01:54:23,082 --> 01:54:24,912
- You kept trying to stop me.
- What did I tell you?

2950
01:54:24,912 --> 01:54:26,582
- You stopped him last time.
- I won't get on the boat.

2951
01:54:26,582 --> 01:54:27,652
You stopped him last time.

2952
01:54:27,652 --> 01:54:29,752
- Then let's do it.
- You can also operate it.

2953
01:54:29,752 --> 01:54:30,922
- It's very easy.
- No, I can't.

2954
01:54:30,922 --> 01:54:32,252
Be clear about it now. If you don't want to ride the boat,

2955
01:54:32,252 --> 01:54:33,492
we can go running.

2956
01:54:33,492 --> 01:54:35,992
What's there not to like when I'm doing it with you?

2957
01:54:35,992 --> 01:54:37,662
- That's right. He's your son.
- My gosh.

2958
01:54:37,662 --> 01:54:38,762
My gosh.

2959
01:54:39,862 --> 01:54:42,202
He's very moved right now.

2960
01:54:42,202 --> 01:54:43,672
I just looked at him from the side.

2961
01:54:43,772 --> 01:54:46,202
- He's truly moved.
- Doing something...

2962
01:54:46,202 --> 01:54:47,642
- with You Seok...
- He's really touched.

2963
01:54:47,772 --> 01:54:49,242
I looked at him briefly...

2964
01:54:49,242 --> 01:54:50,872
from the side.

2965
01:54:50,872 --> 01:54:52,142
He's really touched.

2966
01:54:52,342 --> 01:54:53,342
This is great.

2967
01:54:53,342 --> 01:54:55,042
He was stunned for about three seconds.

2968
01:54:55,069 --> 01:54:57,439
(Finally, it begins.)

2969
01:54:57,439 --> 01:54:59,599
(The siblings' curry battle)

2970
01:54:59,599 --> 01:55:02,009
(Mission! Satisfy Chef Yum!)

2971
01:55:02,009 --> 01:55:04,079
(Roh Yoon Seo, the brazen curry newbie)

2972
01:55:04,079 --> 01:55:05,879
(Kim Sun Young, the curry racer)

2973
01:55:05,879 --> 01:55:07,909
(Park Hae Joon, the curry expert)

2974
01:55:07,909 --> 01:55:09,949
(Kang You Seok, the detail king)

2975
01:55:10,049 --> 01:55:12,279
(It's like the curry special of "Culinary Class Wars.")

2976
01:55:12,649 --> 01:55:14,719
(There is a secret behind this curry.)

2977
01:55:15,019 --> 01:55:16,849
(Guys, help me!)

2978
01:55:16,849 --> 01:55:18,559
(In broad daylight,)

2979
01:55:18,559 --> 01:55:20,789
(a mysterious kidnapping incident takes place?)

2980
01:55:21,089 --> 01:55:23,059
(Forget the peace you've enjoyed so far!)

2981
01:55:23,359 --> 01:55:25,759
(They go back and forth between the kitchen and the field.)

2982
01:55:25,759 --> 01:55:29,229
(The siblings' culinary war is about to begin.)

2983
01:55:29,769 --> 01:55:33,569
(How will this story end?)

2984
01:55:33,769 --> 01:55:36,339
(The second story of the siblings, Taean, South Chungcheong Province)

2985
01:55:36,339 --> 01:55:38,979
(A bit of a shy guy makes his appearance.)

2986
01:55:39,079 --> 01:55:41,009
(I'd say my appearance is my main charm.)

2987
01:55:41,179 --> 01:55:43,179
(This guy is modest as well.)

2988
01:55:43,179 --> 01:55:49,319
(He makes the four siblings' hearts flutter.)

2989
01:55:49,589 --> 01:55:53,859
(Cho Jung Seok will be joining with the siblings.)

2990
01:55:53,859 --> 01:55:56,029
(I won't be able to fall asleep tonight.)
